<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/13439/source/22>
        rdf:type         schema:CreativeWork;
        schema:citation  "“<a href=\"http://web.archive.org/web/20140517062107/http://energy-facts.org/\" data-wpel-link=\"external\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"external noopener noreferrer\">Home</a>,” Energy-Facts.org. Archived May 17, 2014. Archived .pdf on file at DeSmog."^^rdf:HTML .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/13439>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“Coal is now powering the remarkable 21st century socio-economic miracle unfolding in China, where 80% of the global population taken out of poverty in the last 20 years is Chinese. Importantly, this increasing dependence on coal continues apace as India and other developing countries are emerging from the wings to seek a better life for their citizens through coal.”";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/13439/source/22>;
        schema:author            <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/entity/frank-clemente/>;
        schema:claimInterpreter  <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:inLanguage        "English"^^schema:Text;
        schema:publisher         <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:url               "https://www.desmog.com/frank-clemente/" .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/13438/source/21>
        rdf:type         schema:CreativeWork;
        schema:citation  "Dr. Frank Clemente. <a href=\"http://web.archive.org/web/20151211215604/https://www.advancedenergyforlife.com/sites/default/files/Clemente%20Energy%20Poverty%20White%20Paper.pdf\" data-wpel-link=\"external\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"external noopener noreferrer\">“Coal Lifts Billions from Energy Poverty and Increases Access to Low-Cost </a><a href=\"http://web.archive.org/web/20151211215604/https://www.advancedenergyforlife.com/sites/default/files/Clemente%20Energy%20Poverty%20White%20Paper.pdf\" data-wpel-link=\"external\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"external noopener noreferrer\">Electricity at Scale” (PDF)</a>, Advance Energy For Life, February, 2014. <a href=\"//www.desmog.com/wp-content/uploads/files/Clemente%20Energy%20Poverty%20White%20Paper.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener external noreferrer\" data-wpel-link=\"external\">Archived .pdf</a> on file at DeSmog."^^rdf:HTML .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/13438>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "[…] On the other side of the globe, since 1990, China has used coal-based energy to lift 650 million people out of poverty, reduce female illiteracy by almost 80 percent and decrease infant mortality by 70 percent. Clean coal technologies, including the construction of highly efficient supercritical power plants, provide the opportunity for the rest of the developing world to utilize coal to eradicate the specter of energy poverty that haunts billions.”";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/13438/source/21>;
        schema:author            <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/entity/frank-clemente/>;
        schema:claimInterpreter  <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:inLanguage        "English"^^schema:Text;
        schema:publisher         <http://desmog.com/>;
