<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/13344>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“It is true that most of the damage from climate change will not occur in the U.S. but rather in poor countries in equatorial regions – in other words, in regions where failed states, rapacious dictators, and ethnic and religious violence are endemic. The paltry difference in global warming that the US can make by reducing emissions will not help those countries. I believe that we have both a national interest and moral obligation to provide effective, community based aid to those countries to assist them in adaptation.”";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/13344/source/40>;
        schema:author            <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/entity/nera-economic-consulting/>;
