<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/13011>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "”[…] We need regular high-impact media coverage of the findings of leading scientists — not just one or two publications, but we need to have hundreds all over the world. We need to have a high degree of information sharing and cooperation between groups, so that when Vincent Gray for example has an article published in New Zealand, we can take the same piece and we can (say) submit it to newspapers all over North America and Europe.";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/13011/source/>;
        schema:author            <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/entity/international-climate-science-coalition/>;
