<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/12944>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“And then there’s debate. These 31,000 scientists say it’s not happening. You have other scientists say it is happening. and McCain has said a long time ago that the science is settled. Well, I think there is an underlying political problem that is very interesting here. And that is that he, in the way he used his rhetoric, he basically put out of the picture any very serious person who’s concerned about the environment but is skeptical about global warming. So that becomes an impossible&nbsp;thing.";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/12944/source/>;
        schema:author            <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/entity/acton-institute/>;
