<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/12915>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“Well, yeah, I mean, of course, I think climate change is happening. I think it’s being caused by humans. I’ve dedicated the last 20 years of my life to addressing it. My concern is with the just gross misrepresentation of what the best available science says that’s having these severe mental health impacts. So I think it’s possible to be somebody that’s very concerned and wants to take action on climate change and also pushes back against the extreme alarmism that we’ve been&nbsp;seeing.”";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/12915/source/>;
        schema:author            <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/entity/michael-shellenberger/>;
        schema:claimInterpreter  <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:inLanguage        "English"^^schema:Text;
        schema:publisher         <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:url               "https://www.desmog.com/michael-shellenberger/" .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/12914/source/>
        rdf:type         schema:CreativeWork;
        schema:citation  ""^^rdf:HTML .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/12914>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“My view is the drug crisis is objectively a much bigger threat to human life and to civilization than climate change, like we’re adapted really well to climate change. We should do something about it. It’s real. There are risks associated with it. But like, there’s no scenario in the Intergovernmental Panel on Climate Change of Climate Change, killing ninety three thousand Americans a year, that there’s no scenario of it killing of it increasing deaths from natural disasters at all,” Shellenberger claimed in the interview.";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/12914/source/>;
        schema:author            <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/entity/michael-shellenberger/>;
        schema:claimInterpreter  <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:inLanguage        "English"^^schema:Text;
        schema:publisher         <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:url               "https://www.desmog.com/michael-shellenberger/" .

