<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/12684/source/20>
        rdf:type         schema:CreativeWork;
        schema:citation  "Joe Pounder. “<a href=\"http://www.definersdc.com/#!Welcome-To-Definers/xg28x/577be6af0cf2a27045ee82a8\" data-wpel-link=\"external\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"external noopener noreferrer\">Welcome To Definers</a>,” <em>Definers Public Affairs</em>, July 5, 2016. Archived .pdf on file at&nbsp;DeSmog."^^rdf:HTML .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/12684>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "The formation of Definers actually began with the founding of America Rising LLC by Matt Rhoades and myself in 2013. I’ve known Rhoades since 2004 when I was his intern at Bush-Cheney ’04. We’ve worked together on and off for the next decade. After 2012 when he was the campaign manager for Mitt Romney and I was the research director at the Republican National Committee, we decided to start America Rising to focus on opposition research, rapid response communications, and video tracking for political&nbsp;clients.";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/12684/source/20>;
        schema:author            <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/entity/america-rising-llc-pac-america-rising-squared-definers-public-affairs/>;
        schema:claimInterpreter  <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:inLanguage        "English"^^schema:Text;
        schema:publisher         <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:url               "https://www.desmog.com/america-rising-llc-pac-america-rising-squared-definers-public-affairs/" .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/12683/source/14>
        rdf:type         schema:CreativeWork;
        schema:citation  "David M. Drucker. “<a href=\"http://www.washingtonexaminer.com/america-rising-launches-nonprofit-affiliate/article/2568199\" data-wpel-link=\"external\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"external noopener noreferrer\">America Rising launches nonprofit affiliate</a>,” <em>Washington Examiner</em>, July 14, 2015. <a href=\"http://web.archive.org/web/20160725054623/http://www.washingtonexaminer.com/america-rising-launches-nonprofit-affiliate/article/2568199\" data-wpel-link=\"external\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"external noopener noreferrer\">Archived July 25, 2016</a>. Archive.is URL: <a href=\"https://archive.is/2FM1Z\" data-wpel-link=\"external\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"external noopener noreferrer\">https://archive.is/2FM1Z</a>"^^rdf:HTML .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/12683>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "The issues-based 501(c)4 won’t be able to run ads directly attacking political foes the way America Rising does. But the group is permitted to spend roughly half of what it raises on political persuasion, and can run critical spots urging someone like Clinton, the presumptive Democratic presidential nominee, to take positions on particular&nbsp;issues.";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/12683/source/14>;
        schema:author            <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/entity/america-rising-llc-pac-america-rising-squared-definers-public-affairs/>;
        schema:claimInterpreter  <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:inLanguage        "English"^^schema:Text;
        schema:publisher         <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:url               "https://www.desmog.com/america-rising-llc-pac-america-rising-squared-definers-public-affairs/" .

