        schema:url               "https://www.desmog.com/institute-liberty/" .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/12673/source/13>
        rdf:type         schema:CreativeWork;
        schema:citation  "Suzanne Goldenberg and Helena Bengtsson. “<a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2016/jun/13/peabody-energy-coal-mining-climate-change-denial-funding\" data-wpel-link=\"external\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"external noopener noreferrer\">Biggest US coal company funded dozens of groups questioning climate change</a>,” <em>The Guardian, </em>June 13, 2016. <a href=\"http://web.archive.org/web/20160620210630/https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2016/jun/13/peabody-energy-coal-mining-climate-change-denial-funding\" data-wpel-link=\"external\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"external noopener noreferrer\">Archived June 20, 2016</a>. Archive URL: <a href=\"https://archive.ph/pw7On\" data-wpel-link=\"external\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"external noopener noreferrer\">https://archive.ph/pw7On</a>"^^rdf:HTML .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/12673>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“These groups collectively are the heart and soul of climate denial,” said Kert Davies, founder of the Climate Investigation Center, who has spent 20 years tracking funding for climate denial. “It’s the broadest list I have seen of one company funding so many nodes in the denial machine.”";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/12673/source/13>;
        schema:author            <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/entity/institute-liberty/>;
        schema:claimInterpreter  <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:inLanguage        "English"^^schema:Text;
        schema:publisher         <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:url               "https://www.desmog.com/institute-liberty/" .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/12672/source/2>
        rdf:type         schema:CreativeWork;
        schema:citation  "“<a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VzNkmzwCI8w\" data-wpel-link=\"external\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"external noopener noreferrer\">Andrew Langer Talks Climate Change Policy on WITF</a>,” YouTube video uploaded by InstituteForLiberty on February 28, 2010. Archived .mp4 on file at DeSmog."^^rdf:HTML .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/12672>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“What’s the man-made portion of the climate changing? […] You’ve got credible scientists who are saying it’s actually very small. And in point of fact, the changes that we’re going to be making, the proposals we’re making in order to abate that very small part of it, will cost a tremendous amount of money.”";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/12672/source/2>;
        schema:author            <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/entity/institute-liberty/>;
        schema:claimInterpreter  <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:inLanguage        "English"^^schema:Text;
        schema:publisher         <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:url               "https://www.desmog.com/institute-liberty/" .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/12671/source/7>
        rdf:type         schema:CreativeWork;
        schema:citation  "“<a href=\"http://www.theregister.co.uk/2010/09/10/carbon_infrastructure_now_is_ok/\" data-wpel-link=\"external\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"external noopener noreferrer\">All CO2-spewing kit now in existence is OK for the planet</a>,” <em>The Register</em>, September 10, 2010."^^rdf:HTML .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/12671>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“All the carbon-spewing machinery the human race now possesses – powerplants, transportation, boilers, the lot – can be kept running for its entire designed life without any significant ill effects on the planetary ecosystem […]”";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/12671/source/7>;
        schema:author            <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/entity/lewis-page/>;
        schema:claimInterpreter  <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:inLanguage        "English"^^schema:Text;
        schema:publisher         <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:url               "https://www.desmog.com/lewis-page/" .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/12670/source/6>
        rdf:type         schema:CreativeWork;
        schema:citation  "“<a href=\"http://www.theregister.co.uk/2011/12/02/antarctic_ice_sheet_carbon_levels/\" data-wpel-link=\"external\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"external noopener noreferrer\">Antarctic ice formed at CO2 levels much higher than today’s</a>,” <em>The Register</em>, December 2, 2011."^^rdf:HTML .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/12670>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“It would seem that this is highly unlikely [that the Antarctic ice sheet might melt due to global warming] given current and near-future levels of atmospheric CO2: at current rates of increase it will take a century at least to reach 600 ppm, the level at which the ice sheet formed itself, and higher levels would be needed to actually start it melting.”";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/12670/source/6>;
        schema:author            <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/entity/lewis-page/>;
        schema:claimInterpreter  <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:inLanguage        "English"^^schema:Text;
        schema:publisher         <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:url               "https://www.desmog.com/lewis-page/" .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/12669/source/5>
        rdf:type         schema:CreativeWork;
        schema:citation  "“<a href=\"http://www.theregister.co.uk/2012/10/26/edf_energy_price_rises/\" data-wpel-link=\"external\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"external noopener noreferrer\">EDF: We’ll raise bills 11% – but only 2% is due to energy costs!</a>”, <em>The Register</em>, October 26, 2012."^^rdf:HTML .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/12669>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“A vote for that politician [a climate change skeptic] is a vote against this sort of vicious price rise, this sort of stealth tax targeted on ordinary folk who find their energy bills a significant cost – the sort of hit that most of us will find pretty painful, given the current economic climate.”";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/12669/source/5>;
        schema:author            <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/entity/lewis-page/>;
        schema:claimInterpreter  <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:inLanguage        "English"^^schema:Text;
        schema:publisher         <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:url               "https://www.desmog.com/lewis-page/" .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/12668/source/4>
        rdf:type         schema:CreativeWork;
        schema:citation  "Lewis Page. “<a href=\"http://www.theregister.co.uk/2013/01/25/norwegian_co2_warming_shocker/\" data-wpel-link=\"external\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"external noopener noreferrer\">Climate shocker: Carry on as we are until 2050, planet will be FINE</a>,” The Register, January 25, 2013."^^rdf:HTML .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/12668>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“With the recent gradual scientific acceptance – even among scientists who have spent their whole lives studying the subject – that global warming is simply much less significant than had been thought, the chance of anyone caring enough to take action is now even lower.”";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/12668/source/4>;
        schema:author            <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/entity/lewis-page/>;
        schema:claimInterpreter  <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:inLanguage        "English"^^schema:Text;
        schema:publisher         <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:url               "https://www.desmog.com/lewis-page/" .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/12667/source/6>
        rdf:type         schema:CreativeWork;
        schema:citation  "“<a href=\"http://news.heartland.org/newspaper-article/1999/01/01/co2-villain-or-friend-exclusive-interview-keith-e-idso\" data-wpel-link=\"external\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"external noopener noreferrer\">CO2: Villain or Friend? An Exclusive Interview with Keith E. Idso</a>,” <em>The Heartlander</em>, January 1, 1999."^^rdf:HTML .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/12667>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“With this information, in light of the increasing human demands on vegetation, it is my personal opinion that capping CO2 emissions or reducing them to some prior level would be akin to ‘biting the hand that feeds us.’”";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/12667/source/6>;
        schema:author            <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/entity/keith-idso/>;
        schema:claimInterpreter  <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:inLanguage        "English"^^schema:Text;
        schema:publisher         <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:url               "https://www.desmog.com/keith-idso/" .

