<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/12529>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“However, even burning all the economically available fossil fuels would not likely even double current atmospheric CO2 levels – to just 0.08% carbon dioxide, compared to 21% oxygen, 78% nitrogen, 0.9% argon and 0.1% for all other gases except water vapor. And doubling CO2would get us away from the near-famine levels for plants that have prevailed for the past tens of millions of years.";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/12529/source/28>;
