<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/12466>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“For one thing, the ambition of many countries to go carbon-neutral by 2050 does not necessarily mean that it will be achieved. Such a vast change to the economy relies on a combination of new technologies becoming economic on a commercial scale by that date. We still don’t know, for example, how we are going to store energy generated by intermittent wind and solar farms.”";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/12466/source/54>;
        schema:author            <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/entity/ross-clark/>;
