<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/12335>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“As the pro-growth policies of the previous administration drove incredible economic growth, the U.S. improved on environmental measures by providing cleaner air, water, and land, and led the world in reducing greenhouse gas emissions. At the same time, the country became a net energy exporter for the first time in nearly 70 years and rejected lopsided, unenforceable, America- last international agreements such as the Paris Agreement.”";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/12335/source/37>;
        schema:author            <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/entity/america-first-policy-institute-afpi/>;
