<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/12332>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“The current administration’s policies seek to allow government intervention to determine the success of only certain companies, industries, and projects at the expense of others. This approach does not consider the implications for consumer costs, grid resiliency, or energy security. The cancellation of the Keystone XL Pipeline and the threatening of the Dakota Access Pipeline are just two examples of recent actions that have been taken.”";
