<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/12324>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“The debate over the effects of greenhouse emissions and policies to address them is intense, and the Trump administration clearly intends to moderate and reverse many of the regulatory initiatives the Obama administration implemented. One policy discussed broadly is a “carbon” tax on greenhouse gas emissions, as a substitute for the regulatory approach or as a component of a larger tax reform intended to reduce the taxation of capital, often advocated as a revenue-neutral tax shift,” the event description read.";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/12324/source/62>;
