<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/12105>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“We once had a country that had cheap, reliable electricity based on coal. And if you want to pull electricity off the grid and use it, most of it comes from coal. If you want to drive an electric car, it’s not an electric car, it’s a coal car. And we are having a perversion of the language to be able to try to persuade people that they are doing something morally good by sending this nation bankrupt. It is madness,” Plimer said.";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/12105/source/>;
