<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/12016>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“NASA scientists have a strong conflict of interest in that they expect to see warming, and they the more alarm they create, the more money they obtain. This is why climate scientists have no business touching the temperature data. They have no training in signal processing and they have shown repeatedly that they will alter data to suit their needs.”";
