<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/11877>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“The contention that human emissions are now the dominant influence on climate is simply a hypothesis, rather than a universally accepted scientific theory. It is therefore correct, indeed verging on compulsory in the scientific tradition, to be skeptical of those who express certainty that ‘the science is settled’&nbsp;and ‘the debate is over’,” Moore said.";
