<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/11726>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“In fact, moderate warming may actually benefit the earth. Warmer temperatures and increased concentrations of carbon stimulate lush plant growth, while mild weather (as opposed to historically frigid eras) benefits human wellbeing. Bjorn Lomborg, the Danish environmental economist and founder of the Copenhagen Consensus, recognizes the existence of global warming but discounts its harms.”&nbsp;— ";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/11726/source/>;
