<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/11719>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“The earth’s climate is a constantly changing, extremely complex chaotic system, driven by the sun and influenced by numerous external factors including the positions of the other planets in the solar system and cosmic radiation. Many of the factors which influence climate are not well understood. Therefore, while it is reasonable to assume that human activities can influence climate, it is not reasonable to assume that humans could effectively control a complex, chaotic system they do not&nbsp;understand.”";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/11719/source/12>;
        schema:author            <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/entity/national-association-scholars/>;
