<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/11611>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“In 20 years[…]&nbsp;in New York City, we’ll be making some resilient adjustments to the fact that, probably, we will be entering a period of global cooling as a result of the fact that the sun spots are at a very low point, and we could probably look forward in 20 years to, ah, maybe a degree and a half Fahrenheit cooler and we’ll manage. We’re&nbsp;resilient.”";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/11611/source/>;
        schema:author            <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/entity/jay-h-lehr/>;
