<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/11572>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“The problem, whether it’s Fed, Afghanistan, COVID, is that we’ve, we have this sort of, these machines for generating consensus, uniformity, you know, and not asking dissident questions even though they’re super urgent and as far as I can tell, the hour is late for all of these institutions, and it’s more urgent than ever that we find a way to have some of these dissident voices get heard in all these different contexts.”";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/11572/source/>;
        schema:author            <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/entity/peter-thiel/>;
