<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/11545>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“That January, Jesse Jackson had led hundreds of students and faculty in protesting Stanford’s required Western Culture course. ‘Hey hey, ho ho, Western Culture’s got to go!’ the protesters chanted. Stanford soon gutted its core curriculum and caved to the ceaseless demands for ‘diversity,’ but Thiel and the Stanford Review were there to push back. The paper provided well-reasoned opposing views and exposed the intolerance of so many multiculturalists.”";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/11545/source/28>;
        schema:author            <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/entity/peter-thiel/>;
