<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/11397>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "Our climate has always undergone changes. Greenland was named Greenland because its coasts used to be very green. It’s presumptuous to think humans’ impact matters so much in comparison to the frightening geologic history of the earth. And who is to say that last year’s temperature is the perfect optimum? Warmer may be better! More people die in cold waves than heat&nbsp;waves.";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/11397/source/33>;
        schema:author            <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/entity/john-stossel/>;
