<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/11307>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“When regulatory authorities impose overly-burdensome costs, or unnecessarily ban modern drilling techniques [like fracking], the economic contribution from the upstream energy industry is diminished. The costs from diminished economic growth are many and, ironically, can include worst environmental stewardship. The lesson for policy is clear: It is imperative that regulators get the balance right,” he writes.";
