        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "Talking about the IPCC, Idso said ,”They have all these predictions of climate catastrophe, but what it really boils down to is this. When you look at the data, the observed data, you find there is nothing unusual, unnatural, or unprecedented about Earth’s current climate. ” He added, “There is no compelling evidence to conclude that rising CO2 concentrations are heaving a measurable influence on climate.”";
