<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/11144>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "Legates argues that models are just too complex: “There’s 40 different kinds of vegetation around the plant. Now, this shows you just how complex these models are. But what I want to point out is how ridiculous this gets […] we’ve got an unbelievable number of variables to try to keep track of, and then we hit it with a little teeny mallet to see what happens and we bet the farm and all the policy of the future on what that model does with that little, teeny nudge, given the fact it’s got all of these fundamental problems associated with them.” ";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/11144/source/>;
        schema:author            <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/entity/david-legates/>;
        schema:claimInterpreter  <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:inLanguage        "English"^^schema:Text;
        schema:publisher         <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:url               "https://www.desmog.com/david-legates/" .

