<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/11135>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“Delaware’s climate is not changing disastrously. Restricting carbon dioxide will have little impact on our climate . . .&nbsp;a carbon tax assumes that the harm done by carbon dioxide emissions from fossil fuel use exceeds the benefits derived from the fuels and their emissions. There is good reason to think the benefits of the emissions — in enhanced plant growth and hence more abundant and affordable food and a general greening of the planet — could by themselves exceed the costs.”";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/11135/source/18>;
