<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/11057>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“The correlation between CO2 emissions from fossil fuel use and rising concentrations of atmospheric CO2 is taken to constitute evidence that human activities are responsible for climate change. However, there is no straightforward causal link between human fossil fuel use and temperatures, although this remains an area of contention,” van Kooten wrote in a working paper titled “";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/11057/source/17>;
