<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/11052>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "”[…] [T]here are two radically different views on the state of the climate. In the mindset of an “alarmist”, the climate has warmed by a significant amount over the past century and human emissions of carbon dioxide are chiefly to blame. The ‘skeptics’ argue that the warming has been within the range of natural variability and is no cause for concern.";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/11052/source/23>;
