<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/10785/source/8>
        rdf:type         schema:CreativeWork;
        schema:citation  "“<a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Wow09yb2pG8\" rel=\"nofollow external noopener noreferrer\" data-wpel-link=\"external\" target=\"_blank\">Teaser interview of Dr. Samuele Furfari, Speaker at the 4th Annual Symposium, 6 – 8 May, Athens</a>.” YouTube video uploaded by user “HAEE Information,” April 5, 2019. Archived. mp4 on file at DeSmog."^^rdf:HTML .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/10785>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“The energy transition is not an easy task. It will require many, many years. And, for sure, fossil fuels and also nuclear are not over,” Furfari said in the interview. “Greece, like many other EU countries, will remain in this paradigm. We should not dream that tomorrow everything will be 100% renewable.”";
