<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/10739>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "Realizing that this issue is not going to go away, the next best solution in our opinion is for any carbon reduction to be voluntary and let technological advances solve the issue, if it even exists. The least desirable effect would be a carbon tax for mandatory cap and trade program. &nbsp;If this occurs, the following criteria should be used (one that is supported by the Administration and some members of&nbsp;Congress).";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/10739/source/8>;
