        schema:abstract          "It appears that there are “other agendas” driving this issue and that the cost of a negligible reduction in temperature would be tremendous. The Kyoto Accord is used for illustrative purposes because it can be used as a benchmark for costs. Some scientists who favor Kyoto also state that it does not go far enough. A paper titled, Global Warming – A Closer Look At The Numbers, by Monte Kiel states “The Kyoto Protocol calls for mandatory carbon reductions of 30% from developed countries like the ";
