<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/10706/source/17>
        rdf:type         schema:CreativeWork;
        schema:citation  "“<a href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20181123211156/https://www.eike-klima-energie.eu/12-konferenz/programm/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow noopener external noreferrer\" data-wpel-link=\"external\">Program – 12th International Climate and Energy Conference</a>” <em>EIKE. </em>Translated via Google Translate. Archived November 23, 2018. Archive.fo URL: <a href=\"https://archive.fo/NndcT\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener external noreferrer\" data-wpel-link=\"external\">https://archive.fo/NndcT</a>"^^rdf:HTML .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/10706>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“When we have fewer cosmic rays, we actually get a warmer world. And uh, maybe, I mean that’s what we’ve been talking about for the last two days. That part of the 20th century warming might actually be because of changes in solar activity. And this mechanism that I’m talking about today might actually be important, or quite important in, uh, in that, uh, that feature,” Svensmark concluded in his talk.";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/10706/source/17>;
        schema:author            <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/entity/henrik-svensmark/>;
        schema:claimInterpreter  <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:inLanguage        "English"^^schema:Text;
        schema:publisher         <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:url               "https://www.desmog.com/henrik-svensmark/" .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/10705/source/16>
        rdf:type         schema:CreativeWork;
        schema:citation  "Kate Connolly. “<a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2019/may/14/germanys-afd-attacks-greta-thunberg-as-it-embraces-climate-denial\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener external noreferrer\" data-wpel-link=\"external\">Germany’s AfD turns on Greta Thunberg as it embraces climate denial</a>,” <em>The Guardian</em>, May 14, 2019. <a href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20190516174154/https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2019/may/14/germanys-afd-attacks-greta-thunberg-as-it-embraces-climate-denial\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener external noreferrer\" data-wpel-link=\"external\">Archived May 16, 2019</a>. Archive.is URL: <a href=\"https://archive.fo/GM8XL\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener external noreferrer\" data-wpel-link=\"external\">http://archive.is/GM8XL</a>"^^rdf:HTML .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/10705>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“The AfD is using the Bundestag as a stage for its dissemination of climate lies. They invite fake experts to a so-called symposium on climate change to generate content for mass dissemination via social media channels and stir up hatred and anger on the internet. We are experiencing a shift to the right on social media and in society. In a short period of time, the new right has established its own counter-society on climate issues. With troll armies, agitating magazines and the support of climate skeptics like EIKE, it has created its own sphere that is massively underestimated.”";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/10705/source/16>;
        schema:author            <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/entity/henrik-svensmark/>;
        schema:claimInterpreter  <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:inLanguage        "English"^^schema:Text;
        schema:publisher         <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:url               "https://www.desmog.com/henrik-svensmark/" .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/10704/source/11>
        rdf:type         schema:CreativeWork;
        schema:citation  "<em>The Chilling Stars: A New Theory of Climate Change</em>, Totem Books, 2007."^^rdf:HTML .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/10704>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“During the last 100 years cosmic rays became scarcer because unusually vigorous action by the Sun batted away many of them. Fewer cosmic rays meant fewer clouds—and a warmer world.”";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/10704/source/11>;
        schema:author            <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/entity/henrik-svensmark/>;
        schema:claimInterpreter  <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:inLanguage        "English"^^schema:Text;
        schema:publisher         <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:url               "https://www.desmog.com/henrik-svensmark/" .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/10703/source/9>
        rdf:type         schema:CreativeWork;
        schema:citation  "“<a href=\"https://youtu.be/wU1qg8HceGI\" rel=\"nofollow external noopener noreferrer\" data-wpel-link=\"external\" target=\"_blank\">The Connection between Cosmic Rays, Clouds and Climate</a>,” YouTube video uploaded by user “GWPF,” March 16, 2018. Archived .mp4 on file at DeSmog."^^rdf:HTML .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/10703>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“We expect that solar activity should cool the Earth, and it could actually be why the temperatures are not increasing. I mean, they haven’t been increasing for the past twenty years,” Svensmark said.";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/10703/source/9>;
        schema:author            <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/entity/henrik-svensmark/>;
        schema:claimInterpreter  <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:inLanguage        "English"^^schema:Text;
        schema:publisher         <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:url               "https://www.desmog.com/henrik-svensmark/" .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/10702/source/7>
        rdf:type         schema:CreativeWork;
        schema:citation  "Henrik Svensmark. “<a href=\"http://jp.dk/opinion/kronik/article1809681.ece\" data-wpel-link=\"external\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"external noopener noreferrer\">Mens Solen sover</a>.” <em>Jyllands-Posten</em>, September 9, 2009. Reposted and <a href=\"https://wattsupwiththat.com/2009/09/10/svensmark-global-warming-stopped-and-a-cooling-is-beginning-enjoy-global-warming-while-it-lasts/\" data-wpel-link=\"external\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"external noopener noreferrer\">translated by Watts Up With That</a>, September 10, 2009."^^rdf:HTML .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/10702>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“In fact global warming has stopped and a cooling is beginning. No climate model has predicted a cooling of the Earth – quite the contrary. And this means that the projections of future climate are unreliable.”";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/10702/source/7>;
