<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/10628/source/7>
        rdf:type         schema:CreativeWork;
        schema:citation  "“<a href=\"http://www.prnewswire.co.uk/cgi/news/release?id=102114\" data-wpel-link=\"external\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"external noopener noreferrer\">Leading scientist speaks out against UK climate change policy</a>”, (Media Release) <em>PRNewswire</em>, May 9, 2003."^^rdf:HTML .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/10628>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“Fear often dominates discussion about the earth’s climate. Many people have been led to believe that drastic measures are necessary to prevent the risk of negative future outcomes, such as global warming. As such, we now face a situation where politicians are misallocating resources because they are responding to manufactured problems, which are based on public anxiety rather than sound scientific evidence. Ineffective measures like the Kyoto Protocol, built on fear rather than science, will not reduce the future burden of greenhouse gases and will cause many more problems than they solve.”";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/10628/source/7>;
        schema:author            <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/entity/sallie-baliunas/>;
        schema:claimInterpreter  <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:inLanguage        "English"^^schema:Text;
        schema:publisher         <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:url               "https://www.desmog.com/sallie-baliunas/" .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/10627/source/6>
        rdf:type         schema:CreativeWork;
        schema:citation  "“<a href=\"http://research.greenpeaceusa.org/?a=download&amp;d=2609\" data-wpel-link=\"external\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"external noopener noreferrer\">Human Activity Is Not Cause of Global Warming</a>” (Media Release), the George C. Marshall Institute, April 10, 1996. Accessed November 14, 2011."^^rdf:HTML .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/10627>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“The science does not suggest dangerous global warming. If there is any trace at all of a greenhouse warming, it is too small to be seen in the climate record. That means that future warming due to human activities will be quite small –well under one degree C.”";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/10627/source/6>;
        schema:author            <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/entity/sallie-baliunas/>;
        schema:claimInterpreter  <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:inLanguage        "English"^^schema:Text;
        schema:publisher         <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:url               "https://www.desmog.com/sallie-baliunas/" .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/10626/source/5>
        rdf:type         schema:CreativeWork;
        schema:citation  "“Washington Roundtable on Science and Public Policy: Climate History and the Sun” (<a href=\"http://www.marshall.org/pdf/materials/90.pdf\" data-wpel-link=\"external\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"external noopener noreferrer\">PDF</a>), George C. Marshall Institute, June 5, 2001."^^rdf:HTML .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/10626>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“But is it possible that the particular temperature increase observed in the last 100 years is the result of carbon dioxide produced by human activities? The scientific evidence clearly indicates that this is not the case … measurements of atmospheric temperatures made by instruments lofted in satellites and balloons show that no warming has occurred in the atmosphere in the last 50 years. This is just the period in which humanmade carbon dioxide has been pouring into the atmosphere and according to the climate studies, the resultant atmospheric warming should be clearly evident.”";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/10626/source/5>;
        schema:author            <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/entity/sallie-baliunas/>;
        schema:claimInterpreter  <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:inLanguage        "English"^^schema:Text;
        schema:publisher         <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:url               "https://www.desmog.com/sallie-baliunas/" .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/10625/source/33>
        rdf:type         schema:CreativeWork;
        schema:citation  "Christopher Flavelle and Lisa Friedman. “<a href=\"https://www.nytimes.com/2020/10/27/climate/trump-election-climate-noaa.html\" data-wpel-link=\"external\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"external noopener noreferrer\">As Election Nears, Trump Makes a Final Push Against Climate Science</a>,” <em>The New York Times</em>, October 27, 2020. <a href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20201027213312/https://www.nytimes.com/2020/10/27/climate/trump-election-climate-noaa.html\" data-wpel-link=\"external\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"external noopener noreferrer\">Archived October 27, 2020.</a> Archive URL: <a href=\"https://archive.vn/nrsy9\" data-wpel-link=\"external\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"external noopener noreferrer\">https://archive.vn/nrsy9</a>"^^rdf:HTML .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/10625>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“Ms. Curry and the others said that, if Mr. Trump wins re-election, further changes at NOAA would include removing longtime authors of the climate assessment and adding new ones who challenge the degree to which warming is occurring, the extent to which it is caused by human activities and the danger it poses to human health, national security and the economy.”";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/10625/source/33>;
        schema:author            <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/entity/ryan-maue/>;
        schema:claimInterpreter  <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:inLanguage        "English"^^schema:Text;
        schema:publisher         <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:url               "https://www.desmog.com/ryan-maue/" .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/10624/source/22>
        rdf:type         schema:CreativeWork;
        schema:citation  "Andrew Freedman and Jason Samenow. “<a href=\"https://www.washingtonpost.com/weather/2021/01/11/controversial-climate-skeptics-release-papers/\" data-wpel-link=\"external\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"external noopener noreferrer\">Trump officials reassigned by White House after publishing controversial climate papers without approval,</a>” <i>The Washington Post</i>, January 13, 2021. <a href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20210113181137/www.washingtonpost.com/weather/2021/01/11/controversial-climate-skeptics-release-papers/\" data-wpel-link=\"external\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"external noopener noreferrer\">Archived January 13, 2021</a>. Archive URL: <a href=\"https://archive.vn/MNFcx\" data-wpel-link=\"external\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"external noopener noreferrer\">https://archive.vn/MNFcx</a>"^^rdf:HTML .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/10624>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“Science papers from NOAA follow a rigorous peer-reviewed process under agency regulations on scientific publications. NOAA was not involved in the creation or posting online of the climate change flyers that have been allegedly attributed to the Office of Science and Technology Policy, nor does NOAA endorse the flyers. OSTP is investigating the issue,” Smullen said in a statement.";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/10624/source/22>;
        schema:author            <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/entity/ryan-maue/>;
        schema:claimInterpreter  <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:inLanguage        "English"^^schema:Text;
        schema:publisher         <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:url               "https://www.desmog.com/ryan-maue/" .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/10623/source/>
        rdf:type         schema:CreativeWork;
        schema:citation  ""^^rdf:HTML .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/10623>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“Dr. Droegemeier was outraged to learn of the materials that were not shared with or approved by OSTP leadership,” OSTP spokeswoman Kristina Baum said in an email Tuesday afternoon. “He first became aware of the documents when contacted by the press. As a result, Dr. Droegemeier took swift action and the individuals responsible have been relieved of their duties at OSTP.”";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/10623/source/>;
        schema:author            <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/entity/ryan-maue/>;
        schema:claimInterpreter  <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:inLanguage        "English"^^schema:Text;
        schema:publisher         <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:url               "https://www.desmog.com/ryan-maue/" .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/10622/source/17>
        rdf:type         schema:CreativeWork;
        schema:citation  "Ryan Maue. “<a href=\"http://web.archive.org/web/20200922043207/https://www.wsj.com/articles/climate-change-hype-doesnt-help-1505672774\" data-wpel-link=\"external\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"external noopener noreferrer\">Climate Change Hype Doesn’t Help</a>,” <em>The Wall Street Journal</em>, September 17, 2017. Archived September 21, 2020. Archive URL: <a href=\"https://archive.vn/uBG4N\" data-wpel-link=\"external\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"external noopener noreferrer\">https://archive.vn/uBG4N</a>"^^rdf:HTML .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/10622>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“By focusing on whether climate change caused a hurricane, journalists fail to appreciate the complexity of extreme weather events. While most details are still hazy with the best climate modeling tools, the bigger issue than global warming is that more people are choosing to live in coastal areas, where hurricanes certainly will be most destructive,” Maue ";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/10622/source/17>;
        schema:author            <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/entity/ryan-maue/>;
        schema:claimInterpreter  <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:inLanguage        "English"^^schema:Text;
        schema:publisher         <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:url               "https://www.desmog.com/ryan-maue/" .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/10621/source/16>
        rdf:type         schema:CreativeWork;
        schema:citation  "“<a href=\"http://web.archive.org/web/20240325215737/https://cowboystatedaily.com/2023/06/30/oregon-county-sues-oil-and-coal-companies-for-51-billion-dont-think-it-cant-happen-in-wyoming/\" data-wpel-link=\"external\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"external noopener noreferrer\">Oregon County Blames Oil, Coal Companies For Climate Change, Suing For $51 Billion</a>,” <em>Cowboy State Daily</em>, June 30, 2023. Archived March 25, 2024. Archive URL: <a href=\"https://archive.ph/Gm1hS\" data-wpel-link=\"external\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"external noopener noreferrer\">https://archive.ph/Gm1hS</a>"^^rdf:HTML .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/10621>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“During your life, you might experience a one degree Fahrenheit global warming of the Earth. You’re never going to be able to sense that,” Maue said.";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/10621/source/16>;
        schema:author            <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/entity/ryan-maue/>;
        schema:claimInterpreter  <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:inLanguage        "English"^^schema:Text;
        schema:publisher         <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:url               "https://www.desmog.com/ryan-maue/" .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/10620/source/14>
        rdf:type         schema:CreativeWork;
        schema:citation  "“<a href=\"https://www.wsj.com/articles/thirty-years-on-how-well-do-global-warming-predictions-stand-up-1529623442\" data-wpel-link=\"external\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"external noopener noreferrer\">Thirty Years On, How Well Do Global Warming Predictions Stand Up?</a>” Wall Street Journal, June 21, 2018. Archive URL: <a href=\"https://archive.vn/83khp\" data-wpel-link=\"external\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"external noopener noreferrer\">https://archive.vn/83khp</a>"^^rdf:HTML .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/10620>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“Global surface temperature has not increased significantly since 2000, discounting the larger-than-usual El Niño of 2015-16. Assessed by Mr. Hansen’s model, surface temperatures are behaving as if we had capped 18 years ago the carbon-dioxide emissions responsible for the enhanced greenhouse effect. But we didn’t. And it isn’t just Mr. Hansen who got it wrong. Models devised by the United Nations Intergovernmental Panel on Climate Change have, on average, predicted about twice as much warming as has been observed since global satellite temperature monitoring began 40 years ago,” Maue and Michaels wrote.";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/10620/source/14>;
        schema:author            <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/entity/ryan-maue/>;
        schema:claimInterpreter  <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:inLanguage        "English"^^schema:Text;
        schema:publisher         <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:url               "https://www.desmog.com/ryan-maue/" .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/10619/source/22>
        rdf:type         schema:CreativeWork;
        schema:citation  "“<a href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20190702115718/https://talentmarket.org/contact/\" data-wpel-link=\"external\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"external noopener noreferrer\">Contact</a>,” <em>Talent Market</em>. Archived July 2, 2019. Archive.fo URL: <a href=\"http://archive.fo/scdQq\" data-wpel-link=\"external\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"external noopener noreferrer\">http://archive.fo/scdQq</a>"^^rdf:HTML .

