<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/10585>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "Carlson: “In the early 90s and stuff, the assumption was that the sun was not playing a role, and so we don’t need to look at the sun. If you eliminate all the natural variables until only carbon dioxide is left, and that’s pretty much where we’re still at, because by the time you get into the 2000s and it was becoming ";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/10585/source/>;
        schema:author            <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/entity/joe-rogan/>;
        schema:claimInterpreter  <http://desmog.com/>;
