<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/10549>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "Jordan Peterson: “Well, with Bill C16, which was the bill that I was complaining about, or criticizing, let’s say, there’s a variety of surrounding policy documents that are derived from the Ontario Human Rights Commission, and they they indicate quite clearly that you’re to regard biological sex, gender identity, gender expression, and sexual proclivity as varying independently, which, of course, they don’t by any stretch of the imagination. They’re so tightly correlated that, well, you can’t use correlation to imply cause or to infer causality. But Jesus, when the correlations are above 0.95, you have to start wondering if there’s actually not some causal link, and it’s absurd to me that we really even have to have that discussion. But the notion… And this is being taught to school kids. This is&nbsp;";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/10549/source/80>;
        schema:author            <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/entity/joe-rogan/>;
        schema:claimInterpreter  <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:inLanguage        "English"^^schema:Text;
        schema:publisher         <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:url               "https://www.desmog.com/joe-rogan/" .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/10548/source/>
        rdf:type         schema:CreativeWork;
        schema:citation  ""^^rdf:HTML .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/10548>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "Jordan Peterson: “Well, I think it’s partly. It’s partly a form of narcissism.”";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/10548/source/>;
        schema:author            <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/entity/joe-rogan/>;
