<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/10356>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“There IS a problem with global warming. […] it stopped in 1998. […] That industrial carbon dioxide is not the primary cause of earth’s recent decadal-scale temperature changes doesn’t seem at all odd to many thousands of independent scientists. They have long appreciated – ever since the early 1990s, when the global warming bandwagon first started to roll behind the gravy train of the UN Intergovernmental Panel on Climate Change (IPCC) – that such short-term climate fluctuations are chiefly of natural origin.”";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/10356/source/12>;
        schema:author            <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/entity/bob-carter/>;
        schema:claimInterpreter  <http://desmog.com/>;
