<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/10091/source/14>
        rdf:type         schema:CreativeWork;
        schema:citation  "D. Brady Nelson. “ <a href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20150726182801/http://news.heartland.org/newspaper-article/2015/07/14/global-warming-policies-reflect-false-assumptions-panelists-say\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener external noreferrer\" data-wpel-link=\"external\">Global Warming Policies Reflect False Assumptions, Panelists Say</a>,” The Heartland Institute, July 14, 2015. Archived July 26, 2015."^^rdf:HTML .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/10091>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“Warming is not serious,” Singer said. “We can stand warming. Ice ages are serious. Major ones come every 100,000 years, controlled by astronomical factors. Not much we can do about those. And there are little ice ages, and they come about every 1,000–1,500 years. The major ice ages nearly wiped out humanity, at least they nearly did in Europe. … They wiped out the Neanderthals.”";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/10091/source/14>;
        schema:author            <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/entity/science-and-environmental-policy-project/>;
