<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/10086>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“Innovation that has dramatically reduced the cost of solar and wind energy is a big part of the story. But it is also a fact that much of the electricity decarbonization has taken because of the natural gas revolution that has reduced coal use. Furthermore, the ability of natural gas to respond to the variability of solar and wind is critical for maintaining a reliable and resilient system,” Moniz and Karsner wrote.";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/10086/source/>;
