<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/9993>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“I’m not looking for people who wish to earn a four-year degree, or individuals in pursuit of their ‘dream job.’ With respect, I don’t care about your dreams. Nor do I care about you IQ, your test scores, your athletic prowess, your artistic ability, or any of the other things most other scholarship programs concern themselves with. I care about your attitude, your work ethic, your commitment to personal responsibility, and your desire to master a trade.”";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/9993/source/23>;
        schema:author            <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/entity/mike-rowe/>;
        schema:claimInterpreter  <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:inLanguage        "English"^^schema:Text;
        schema:publisher         <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:url               "https://www.desmog.com/mike-rowe/" .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/9992/source/22>
        rdf:type         schema:CreativeWork;
        schema:citation  "“<a href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20210426225138/https://www.mikeroweworks.org/about/\" data-wpel-link=\"external\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"external noopener noreferrer\">About</a>,” <em>mikeroweWORKS Foundation. </em>Archived April 26, 2021. Archive URL: <a href=\"https://archive.ph/jQI2L\" data-wpel-link=\"external\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"external noopener noreferrer\">https://archive.ph/jQI2L</a>"^^rdf:HTML .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/9992>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“Our crumbling infrastructure, our widening skills gap, the disappearance of vocational education, and the stratospheric rise in college tuition—these are not problems,” Rowe said. “These are symptoms of what we value. And right now, we have to reconnect the average American with the value of a skilled workforce. Only then, will the next generation aspire to do the work at hand.”";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/9992/source/22>;
        schema:author            <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/entity/mike-rowe/>;
        schema:claimInterpreter  <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:inLanguage        "English"^^schema:Text;
        schema:publisher         <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:url               "https://www.desmog.com/mike-rowe/" .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/9991/source/>
        rdf:type         schema:CreativeWork;
        schema:citation  ""^^rdf:HTML .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/9991>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“In short, we found ourselves in violent agreement on a number of things important to us both, and after lunch, he told me to let him know if mikeroweWORKS could ever use his help. (In hindsight, it’s entirely possible he was just being polite, but he would soon learn just how literal I can be.)”";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/9991/source/>;
        schema:author            <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/entity/mike-rowe/>;
        schema:claimInterpreter  <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:inLanguage        "English"^^schema:Text;
        schema:publisher         <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:url               "https://www.desmog.com/mike-rowe/" .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/9990/source/>
        rdf:type         schema:CreativeWork;
        schema:citation  ""^^rdf:HTML .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/9990>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“But I was most surprised by his commitment to reinvigorate the skilled trades. I knew his foundation focused on many forms of higher education, but I had no idea we shared a common view regarding the skills gap. He pointed out that countless small businesses begin with a tradesperson who learned a skill that was in demand. I shared my belief that a chronic skills gap was more troubling than chronic unemployment, because the existence of opportunity that people don’t care about is more alarming than a lack of opportunity overall.";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/9990/source/>;
        schema:author            <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/entity/mike-rowe/>;
        schema:claimInterpreter  <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:inLanguage        "English"^^schema:Text;
        schema:publisher         <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:url               "https://www.desmog.com/mike-rowe/" .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/9989/source/>
        rdf:type         schema:CreativeWork;
        schema:citation  ""^^rdf:HTML .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/9989>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“We met a few years ago in California. I had just given a speech about the disastrous consequences of removing vocational education from high schools, and Charles was in the audience. One of his people invited me to lunch, and I said sure. I was eager to see the horns and smell the sulphur for myself. Surprisingly, I found neither. What I found, was a 78-year-old man with more energy and enthusiasm than I could match. We spoke at length, and I learned a number of surprising things. […] I learned for instance, about his passion for criminal justice reform.";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/9989/source/>;
        schema:author            <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/entity/mike-rowe/>;
        schema:claimInterpreter  <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:inLanguage        "English"^^schema:Text;
        schema:publisher         <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:url               "https://www.desmog.com/mike-rowe/" .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/9988/source/9>
        rdf:type         schema:CreativeWork;
        schema:citation  "Edward E. David Jr. “Science Futures: The Industrial Connection,”<em> Science</em>, 203(4383), March 2, 1979: 837. Quoted in “Big Oil U.” (<a href=\"http://cspinet.org/new/pdf/bigoilu.pdf\" data-wpel-link=\"external\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"external noopener noreferrer\">PDF</a>), Center for Science in the Public Interest."^^rdf:HTML .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/9988>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“The time has come for a closer and more intimate relationship between industry and academia.”";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/9988/source/9>;
        schema:author            <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/entity/edward-david/>;
