        schema:citation  "<a name=\"s1\" id=\"s1\"></a>“<a href=\"http://fizz.phys.dal.ca/people/PChylek/PChylek.html\" data-wpel-link=\"external\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"external noopener noreferrer\">Petr Chylek: Professor of Physics and Atmospheric Science</a>,” Dalhousie University. Accessed December 2, 2011."^^rdf:HTML .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/9794>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“A common view on the current climate change (global warming) is that it is a result of fossil fuel burning and the following increase in atmospheric concentration of carbon dioxide. In reality there are several factors that produce the current climate change. Some of the most important are:";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/9794/source/6>;
        schema:author            <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/entity/petr-chylek/>;
