        rdf:type         schema:CreativeWork;
        schema:citation  "“<a href=\"http://www.juandemariana.org/article/976/zp/terrorism/and/climate/change/\" data-wpel-link=\"external\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"external noopener noreferrer\">ZP on Terrorism and Climate Change</a>,” Instituto Juan de Mariana, 2006/11/05."^^rdf:HTML .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/9669>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“[S]cientists are still uncertain how much human activity, through Co2 emissions, might be contributing to climate change in comparison to other factors like water vapour or solar activity. There is, however, a scientific consensus on the fact that, even if we froze carbon dioxide emissions as the Kyoto Protocol intended, warming would decrease barely 0.07 degrees centigrade.”";
