<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/9490>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“It’s worth remembering why we are doing this. It’s certainly not going to make any difference to the Earth’s temperature: our carbon dioxide emissions are a tiny fraction of the global total, and smaller than annual increases in China and India. No, we are doing this as a gesture: a way to show our leadership on climate change, setting an example to the rest of the&nbsp;world.”";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/9490/source/>;
        schema:author            <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/entity/global-warming-policy-foundation/>;
        schema:claimInterpreter  <http://desmog.com/>;
