<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/9489/source/198>
        rdf:type         schema:CreativeWork;
        schema:citation  "“<a href=\"http://web.archive.org/web/20191202152803/https://www.thegwpf.org/clive-james-legendary-author-poet-humorist-climate-sceptic-has-died/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener external noreferrer\" data-wpel-link=\"external\">Clive James, Legendary Author, Poet, Humorist &amp; Climate Sceptic Has Died</a>,” <em>The Global Warming Policy Foundation</em>, November 27, 2019. Archived December 2, 2019. Archive URL:&nbsp;<a href=\"http://archive.md/7a2J5\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener external noreferrer\" data-wpel-link=\"external\">http://archive.md/7a2J5</a>"^^rdf:HTML .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/9489>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“…this particular area has a knack of raising questions that get more and more complicated in the absence of an answer to the elementary ones. One of those elementary questions is about how man-made carbon dioxide can be a driver of climate change if the global temperature has not gone up by much over the last twenty years but the amount of man-made carbon dioxide has. If we go on to ask a supplementary question – say, how could carbon dioxide raise temperature when the evidence of the ice cores indicates that temperature has always raised carbon dioxide – we will be given complicated answers, but we still haven’t had an answer to the first question, except for the suggestion that the temperature, despite the observations, really has gone up, but that the extra heat is hiding in the&nbsp;ocean.”";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/9489/source/198>;
        schema:author            <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/entity/global-warming-policy-foundation/>;
        schema:claimInterpreter  <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:inLanguage        "English"^^schema:Text;
        schema:publisher         <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:url               "https://www.desmog.com/global-warming-policy-foundation/" .

