<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/9299>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“Surface temperatures are indeed increasing slightly: They’ve been going up, in fits and starts, for more than 150 years, or since a miserably cold and pestilential period known as the Little Ice Age. Before carbon dioxide from economic activity could have warmed us up, temperatures rose three-quarters of a degree Fahrenheit between 1910 and World War ";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/9299/source/22>;
