        rdf:type         schema:CreativeWork;
        schema:citation  "“<a href=\"https://archive.fo/lx7Gk\" data-wpel-link=\"external\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"external noopener noreferrer\">The So-Called ‘Greenhouse Effect’ is a Myth</a>,” <i>ICECAP</i>, July 14, 2008. Archived October 10, 2019."^^rdf:HTML .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/9294>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“As a dissenting physicist, I simply can no longer buy the notion that CO2 produces any significant warming of the atmosphere at any rate. I’ve studied the atomic absorption physics to death, from John Nicol’s extensive development to the much longer winded dissertation by Gerlich &amp; Tscheuschner and everything in between, it simply doesn’t add up. Even if every single IR photon absorbed by a CO2 molecule were magically transformed into purely thermal translational modes , the pitifully small quantity of CO2 in the atmosphere doesn’t add up to much additional heat. And if the aforementioned magical 100% transformation from radiation into “heat” were true, then all arguments concerning re-emission ( source of all the wonderful “greenhouse effect” cartoons with their arrows flying in all directions ) are out the window.";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/9294/source/10>;
        schema:author            <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/entity/james-peden/>;
        schema:claimInterpreter  <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:inLanguage        "English"^^schema:Text;
        schema:publisher         <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:url               "https://www.desmog.com/james-peden/" .

