<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/9211/source/54>
        rdf:type         schema:CreativeWork;
        schema:citation  "Fredrick D. Palmer. “<a href=\"http://web.archive.org/web/20170113195117/https://www.pop.org/content/so-what-about-global-warming\" data-wpel-link=\"external\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"external noopener noreferrer\">So, what about this global warming?</a>” <em>Population Research Institute</em>, December 1, 1998. Archived January 13, 2017. Archive.is URL: <a href=\"https://archive.is/2WpR4\" data-wpel-link=\"external\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"external noopener noreferrer\">https://archive.is/2WpR4</a>"^^rdf:HTML .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/9211>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“Carbon dioxide is no pollutant; it is the foundation of life on earth,” Palmer writes. Describing his work with the Western Fuels Association, Palmer says “We work in the public interest from end-to-end.”";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/9211/source/54>;
        schema:author            <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/entity/fred-palmer/>;
        schema:claimInterpreter  <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:inLanguage        "English"^^schema:Text;
        schema:publisher         <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:url               "https://www.desmog.com/fred-palmer/" .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/9210/source/53>
        rdf:type         schema:CreativeWork;
        schema:citation  "“<a href=\"http://web.archive.org/web/20170111204432/http://www.pbs.org/wgbh/warming/debate/palmer.html\" data-wpel-link=\"external\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"external noopener noreferrer\">Interview: Fred Palmer</a>,” <em>PBS</em>. Archived January 11, 2017. Archive.is URL: <a href=\"https://archive.is/89KWu\" data-wpel-link=\"external\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"external noopener noreferrer\">https://archive.is/89KWu</a>"^^rdf:HTML .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/9210>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“We are at the top of the food chain insofar as CO2 emissions are concerned. So if you get in the business of limiting CO2 emissions, of taxing CO2 emissions, of creating a value in CO2 emissions where people trade them in this emissions trading scheme, you go to the coal plants first because of the fact that that’s the greatest source –single source–of CO2 that there is.”";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/9210/source/53>;
        schema:author            <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/entity/fred-palmer/>;
        schema:claimInterpreter  <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:inLanguage        "English"^^schema:Text;
        schema:publisher         <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:url               "https://www.desmog.com/fred-palmer/" .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/9209/source/53>
        rdf:type         schema:CreativeWork;
        schema:citation  "“<a href=\"http://web.archive.org/web/20170111204432/http://www.pbs.org/wgbh/warming/debate/palmer.html\" data-wpel-link=\"external\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"external noopener noreferrer\">Interview: Fred Palmer</a>,” <em>PBS</em>. Archived January 11, 2017. Archive.is URL: <a href=\"https://archive.is/89KWu\" data-wpel-link=\"external\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"external noopener noreferrer\">https://archive.is/89KWu</a>"^^rdf:HTML .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/9209>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“[T]he science to me–and I have been involved, not as a scientist but as a lawyer–the science to me suggests, in the ten years I’ve been involved in it, that there is no basis, no mechanism that anybody can point to or look at to say that more CO2 in the air is going to lead to catastrophic global warming or apocalyptic global warming, as opposed to some mild warming, which is nothing to be concerned about at all.”";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/9209/source/53>;
        schema:author            <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/entity/fred-palmer/>;
        schema:claimInterpreter  <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:inLanguage        "English"^^schema:Text;
        schema:publisher         <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:url               "https://www.desmog.com/fred-palmer/" .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/9208/source/53>
        rdf:type         schema:CreativeWork;
        schema:citation  "“<a href=\"http://web.archive.org/web/20170111204432/http://www.pbs.org/wgbh/warming/debate/palmer.html\" data-wpel-link=\"external\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"external noopener noreferrer\">Interview: Fred Palmer</a>,” <em>PBS</em>. Archived January 11, 2017. Archive.is URL: <a href=\"https://archive.is/89KWu\" data-wpel-link=\"external\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"external noopener noreferrer\">https://archive.is/89KWu</a>"^^rdf:HTML .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/9208>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“[T]he precautionary principle might say that we should put more CO2 in the air to prevent CO2 levels from being driven down to such low levels in the future by an ice age that it extinguishes plant life. And there are scientists that believe this.”";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/9208/source/53>;
        schema:author            <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/entity/fred-palmer/>;
        schema:claimInterpreter  <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:inLanguage        "English"^^schema:Text;
        schema:publisher         <http://desmog.com/>;
