<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/9185>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“Coal is not dirty. Coal is green. And I say that because coal is electricity, and electricity at the point of use is the cleanest, most efficient form of energy,” Palmer said at the Heartland Institute’s America First energy conference. “Coal is green. It is not dirty, because of electrification. CO2 is a benign gas required for life on Earth and is not dirty.”";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/9185/source/39>;
        schema:author            <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/entity/fred-palmer/>;
