<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/9180>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "What about ‘global warming?’ What matters is the degree and rate of change. There have been times on earth when it has been much warmer than today, and times when it’s been much colder. The latter are called ice ages. One of the former is called ‘The Climate Optimum.’ It was a time of higher average global temperature and high CO2.”";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/9180/source/34>;
        schema:author            <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/entity/fred-palmer/>;
