<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/9101>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“There used to be a large number of fires in the early part of the 20th Century and before that,” Mass said. “People don’t realize that this used to be a very smoky place because we have forests all around us. There used to be fires all the time. So smoke is not unknown around&nbsp;here.”";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/9101/source/>;
        schema:author            <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/entity/clifford-mass/>;
        schema:claimInterpreter  <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:inLanguage        "English"^^schema:Text;
        schema:publisher         <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:url               "https://www.desmog.com/clifford-mass/" .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/9100/source/>
        rdf:type         schema:CreativeWork;
        schema:citation  ""^^rdf:HTML .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/9100>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“So what is unusual is that we suppressed the fires for almost 100 years. So people got used to the fact there weren’t a lot of fires and smoke, but that’s the natural state around here.”";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/9100/source/>;
        schema:author            <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/entity/clifford-mass/>;
        schema:claimInterpreter  <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:inLanguage        "English"^^schema:Text;
        schema:publisher         <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:url               "https://www.desmog.com/clifford-mass/" .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/9099/source/>
        rdf:type         schema:CreativeWork;
        schema:citation  ""^^rdf:HTML .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/9099>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“Well, number one is we have to fix our forests up. You know, some people say this is climate change or something else, but the key thing is probably not climate change. It’s that we have these forests that we’ve suppressed fires for one-hundred years and they are totally messed up. They are completely overgrown—dense growth that is completely unnatural.”";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/9099/source/>;
        schema:author            <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/entity/clifford-mass/>;
