<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/9072>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“Wind power is not only bird-killing, noise-polluting, eyesore-causing, cost-prohibiting and vegetative-decreasing, but its intermittency leads to periods of overproduction or power shortages that necessitate reliance on traditional technologies as back-up or on costly storage technologies,” the IER report concluded.";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/9072/source/66>;
