<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/9050>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "ALEC is a corporate bill mill. It is not just a lobby or a front group; it is much more powerful than that. Through ALEC, corporations hand state legislators their wishlists to benefit their bottom line. Corporations fund almost all of ALEC’s operations. They pay for a seat on ALEC task forces where corporate lobbyists and special interest reps vote with elected officials to approve “model”&nbsp;bills.";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/9050/source/>;
        schema:author            <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/entity/institute-energy-research/>;
