<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/8968>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "Because many of the First Nations and environmental groups funded through the Moore Foundation also opposed the Enbridge Northern Gateway pipeline, on the strength of this correlation alone, it’s now claimed that the true purpose of Moore’s grants was not environmental protection but protection of the American trade monopoly on Canadian oil. […] One of the most disgraceful episodes of Canada’s recent political history is the casual and baseless besmirching of stellar reputations like the Moore Foundation’s in pursuit of tortuous and convoluted conjecture by a single researcher, now elevated to official government policy.”";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/8968/source/89>;
