        rdf:type         schema:CreativeWork;
        schema:citation  "Kate Webb. “<a href=\"http://www.metronews.ca/news/vancouver/2012/06/04/north-van-writer-wants-u-s-charity-money-out-of-canada.html\" data-wpel-link=\"external\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"external noopener noreferrer\">North Van writer wants U.S. charity money out of Canada</a>,” <em>Metro Vancouver</em>, June 4, 2012. <a href=\"http://web.archive.org/web/20171110191651/http://www.metronews.ca/news/vancouver/2012/06/04/north-van-writer-wants-u-s-charity-money-out-of-canada.html\" data-wpel-link=\"external\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"external noopener noreferrer\">Archived November 10, 2017</a>. Archive.is URL: <a href=\"https://archive.is/ZnBUJ\" data-wpel-link=\"external\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"external noopener noreferrer\">https://archive.is/ZnBUJ</a>"^^rdf:HTML .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/8905>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“The amount of money coming from foreign sources to Canadian environmental groups seems really small compared to foreign investment in and ownership of key Canadian industries, the impact of foreign demand for our exports on the ways we’re developing our lands … and the kinds of environmental risks, so it’s a very selective voicing of concerns about the impact of foreign funding on Canadian politics.”";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/8905/source/187>;
        schema:author            <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/entity/vivian-m-krause/>;
        schema:claimInterpreter  <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:inLanguage        "English"^^schema:Text;
        schema:publisher         <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:url               "https://www.desmog.com/vivian-m-krause/" .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/8904/source/>
        rdf:type         schema:CreativeWork;
        schema:citation  ""^^rdf:HTML .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/8904>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“I can imagine foreign money in Canadian politics being really problematic if that influence was outweighing the influence of Canadians with their own resources, but certainly in the case of the environmental movement, we’re so far from that,” she said.";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/8904/source/>;
        schema:author            <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/entity/vivian-m-krause/>;
        schema:claimInterpreter  <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:inLanguage        "English"^^schema:Text;
        schema:publisher         <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:url               "https://www.desmog.com/vivian-m-krause/" .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/8903/source/190>
        rdf:type         schema:CreativeWork;
        schema:citation  "“<a href=\"http://www.huffingtonpost.ca/2012/06/07/krause-charities-us-interests_n_1578244.html\" data-wpel-link=\"external\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"external noopener noreferrer\">Vivian Krause Alleges Foreign Funded Green Charities Boost American Finances</a>,” <em>HuffPost</em>, June 7, 2012. <a href=\"http://web.archive.org/web/20171109204811/http://www.huffingtonpost.ca/2012/06/07/krause-charities-us-interests_n_1578244.html\" data-wpel-link=\"external\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"external noopener noreferrer\">Archived November 9, 2017</a>. Archive.is URL: <a href=\"https://archive.is/E4ULC\" data-wpel-link=\"external\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"external noopener noreferrer\">https://archive.is/E4ULC</a>"^^rdf:HTML .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/8903>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“We are a Canadian organization, run by Canadians, on behalf of Canadians and we are absolutely working on behalf of Canadians. We don’t respond to outside foreign agendas,” Goodman said via phone. “I don’t believe that (foreign foundations have other interests at play). I think it’s a conspiracy theory and I think it’s a red herring,” she said.";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/8903/source/190>;
        schema:author            <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/entity/vivian-m-krause/>;
        schema:claimInterpreter  <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:inLanguage        "English"^^schema:Text;
        schema:publisher         <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:url               "https://www.desmog.com/vivian-m-krause/" .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/8902/source/194>
        rdf:type         schema:CreativeWork;
        schema:citation  "“<a href=\"http://www.ourcommons.ca/DocumentViewer/en/41-1/RNNR/meeting-25/evidence\" data-wpel-link=\"external\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"external noopener noreferrer\">Evidence: THURSDAY, FEBRUARY 9, 2012</a>,”<em> House of Commons Standing Committee on Natural Resources</em>, February 9, 2012. <a href=\"http://web.archive.org/web/20171109191155/http://www.ourcommons.ca/DocumentViewer/en/41-1/RNNR/meeting-25/evidence\" data-wpel-link=\"external\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"external noopener noreferrer\">Archived November 9, 2017</a>. Archive.is URL: <a href=\"https://archive.is/mDQEr\" data-wpel-link=\"external\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"external noopener noreferrer\">https://archive.is/mDQEr</a>"^^rdf:HTML .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/8902>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“The campaign to shift from dirty to clean energy, as it appears to me, is also about reducing dependence on imported oil, and increasing energy independence. In fact, if you read the fine print, you will find that American foundations say this themselves in their strategy papers, that one of their interests is in increasing American energy security and American energy independence.”";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/8902/source/194>;
        schema:author            <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/entity/vivian-m-krause/>;
        schema:claimInterpreter  <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:inLanguage        "English"^^schema:Text;
        schema:publisher         <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:url               "https://www.desmog.com/vivian-m-krause/" .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/8901/source/>
        rdf:type         schema:CreativeWork;
        schema:citation  ""^^rdf:HTML .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/8901>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“As I see it, the campaign against Canadian energy is one side of a two-sided coin. The other side of the coin is the creation of the renewable energy industry,” Krause said in her testimony. “Of course, the dichotomy between dirty and clean energy is a bit of a false dichotomy in the sense that the so-called clean energy industry also has some negative environmental impacts. Underneath this dichotomy is another dichotomy, which of course is between energy that has historically been largely or partially from foreign oil imports and an industry that has been created that is primarily domestic.";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/8901/source/>;
        schema:author            <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/entity/vivian-m-krause/>;
        schema:claimInterpreter  <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:inLanguage        "English"^^schema:Text;
        schema:publisher         <http://desmog.com/>;
