<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/8837>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“Reducing artificially high energy costs is the first step in tackling fuel poverty. In America, the market is alleviating the burden of energy costs on poor households, even as the government goes the wrong way. That shows us the way forward for tackling the much greater problem in the developing world.”";
