<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/8732/source/17>
        rdf:type         schema:CreativeWork;
        schema:citation  "<a name=\"s11\"></a>S. Fred Singer. “<a href=\"http://web.archive.org/web/20160913232622/http://www.washingtontimes.com/news/2015/jan/21/s-fred-singer-global-climate-policy-after-lima/\" data-wpel-link=\"external\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"external noopener noreferrer\">Global climate policy after Lima</a>,” <em>The Washington Times</em>, January 21, 2015. Archived September 13, 2016. Archive.is URL: <a href=\"https://archive.is/F1O74\" data-wpel-link=\"external\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"external noopener noreferrer\">https://archive.is/F1O74</a>"^^rdf:HTML .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/8732>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“More specifically, on the climate-energy issue, [Republican Senator Chuck] Hagel can point to increasing evidence that nature rules the climate — and always has — not human activities. He can point to the disastrous record of Kyoto and scandalous waste of resources and human efforts — and how ‘saving the climate’ detracts from solving genuine world problems.";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/8732/source/17>;
        schema:author            <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/entity/s-fred-singer/>;
        schema:claimInterpreter  <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:inLanguage        "English"^^schema:Text;
        schema:publisher         <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:url               "https://www.desmog.com/s-fred-singer/" .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/8731/source/16>
        rdf:type         schema:CreativeWork;
        schema:citation  "<a name=\"s10\"></a>S. Fred Singer. “<a href=\"http://web.archive.org/web/20160913234139/http://www.americanthinker.com/articles/2016/02/the_goldilocks_approach_to_global_warming.html\" data-wpel-link=\"external\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"external noopener noreferrer\">The Goldilocks Approach to Global Warming</a>,” <em>American Thinker</em>, February 8, 2016. Archived September 13, 2016. Archive.is URL: <a href=\"https://archive.is/Qm8PI\" data-wpel-link=\"external\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"external noopener noreferrer\">https://archive.is/Qm8PI</a>"^^rdf:HTML .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/8731>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“I go back to the major error of the UN climate panel, the Intergovernmental Panel on Climate Change (IPCC). They have been claiming in all their 5 major reports that CO2 increases are the cause of warming. I am of the opinion, and have tried to back it up with publications, that these arguments don’t hold water and that their evidence does not exist.”";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/8731/source/16>;
        schema:author            <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/entity/s-fred-singer/>;
        schema:claimInterpreter  <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:inLanguage        "English"^^schema:Text;
        schema:publisher         <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:url               "https://www.desmog.com/s-fred-singer/" .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/8730/source/15>
        rdf:type         schema:CreativeWork;
        schema:citation  "“<a href=\"http://web.archive.org/web/20161017175732/http://www.pbs.org/wgbh/warming/debate/singer.html\" data-wpel-link=\"external\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"external noopener noreferrer\">Interview: Dr. S. Fred Singer</a>,” PBS.org. Archived Ocober 17, 2016. Archive.is URL: <a href=\"https://archive.is/Rvtwq\" data-wpel-link=\"external\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"external noopener noreferrer\">https://archive.is/Rvtwq</a>"^^rdf:HTML .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/8730>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“Climate change is a natural phenomenon. Climate keeps changing all the time. The fact that climate changes is not in itself a threat, because, obviously, in the past human beings have adapted to all kinds of climate changes.”";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/8730/source/15>;
        schema:author            <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/entity/s-fred-singer/>;
        schema:claimInterpreter  <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:inLanguage        "English"^^schema:Text;
        schema:publisher         <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:url               "https://www.desmog.com/s-fred-singer/" .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/8729/source/14>
        rdf:type         schema:CreativeWork;
        schema:citation  "<a name=\"s9\"></a>“<a href=\"http://www.nature.com/nature/journal/v478/n7370/full/478428a.html\" data-wpel-link=\"external\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"external noopener noreferrer\">Scientific climate</a>,” <em>Nature </em>478, 428 (27 October 2011). See Singer’s comment, <a href=\"http://www.nature.com/nature/journal/v478/n7370/full/478428a.html#comment-28687\" data-wpel-link=\"external\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"external noopener noreferrer\">“Dear Editors of Nature:,” Comment #28687</a>. Archived image on file at Desmog."^^rdf:HTML .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/8729>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“[U]nlike the land surface, the atmosphere has shown no warming trend, either over land or over ocean — according to satellites and independent data from weather balloons.”";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/8729/source/14>;
        schema:author            <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/entity/s-fred-singer/>;
        schema:claimInterpreter  <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:inLanguage        "English"^^schema:Text;
        schema:publisher         <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:url               "https://www.desmog.com/s-fred-singer/" .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/8728/source/12>
        rdf:type         schema:CreativeWork;
        schema:citation  "<a name=\"s7\"></a>S. Fred Singer. “<a href=\"http://web.archive.org/web/20160913232902/http://www.americanthinker.com/articles/2015/06/the_climate_warming_pause_goes_awol.html\" data-wpel-link=\"external\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"external noopener noreferrer\">The climate warming pause goes AWOL (or not)</a>,” <em>American Thinker</em>, June 4, 2015. Archived September 13, 2016. Archive.is URL: <a href=\"https://archive.is/MslNm\" data-wpel-link=\"external\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"external noopener noreferrer\">https://archive.is/MslNm</a>"^^rdf:HTML .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/8728>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "One thing is quite certain, however: Current IPCC climate models cannot explain what the observations clearly show. This makes the models unsuitable for climate prediction – and for policy purposes generally.”";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/8728/source/12>;
        schema:author            <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/entity/s-fred-singer/>;
        schema:claimInterpreter  <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:inLanguage        "English"^^schema:Text;
        schema:publisher         <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:url               "https://www.desmog.com/s-fred-singer/" .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/8727/source/>
        rdf:type         schema:CreativeWork;
        schema:citation  ""^^rdf:HTML .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/8727>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "There will certainly be debate also about my proposition of no evidence at all for AGW.We will need a persuasive answer to the puzzle — why do land thermometers show a warming before 2000, but not after 2000?I may have an answer, but must first try to convince my colleagues.";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/8727/source/>;
        schema:author            <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/entity/s-fred-singer/>;
