        rdf:type         schema:CreativeWork;
        schema:citation  "“<a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=K12PCuBjFgI\" data-wpel-link=\"external\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"external noopener noreferrer\">Scott Pruitt 2014 ALEC Annual Meeting</a>,” YouTube video uploaded by user American Legislative Exchange Council (ALEC), August 5, 2014. Archived .mp4 on file at DeSmog."^^rdf:HTML .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/8618>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“Beyond the regional haze case, we have something on the horizon something more troubling. And that’s the proposed rule under 111(d) with respect to CO2 regulation. We have an EPA that is engaged in rulemaking, proposed rulemaking, that seeks to exert itself in a way that the statute doesn’t authorize at all.”";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/8618/source/76>;
        schema:author            <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/entity/scott-pruitt/>;
        schema:claimInterpreter  <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:inLanguage        "English"^^schema:Text;
        schema:publisher         <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:url               "https://www.desmog.com/scott-pruitt/" .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/8617/source/75>
        rdf:type         schema:CreativeWork;
        schema:citation  "“<a href=\"http://wypr.org/post/pick-epa-administrator-opposed-federal-chesapeake-bay-cleanup\" data-wpel-link=\"external\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"external noopener noreferrer\">Pick for EPA Administrator Opposed Federal Chesapeake Bay Cleanup</a>,” WYPR, December 21, 2016. Archive.is URL: <a href=\"https://archive.is/SVI6R\" data-wpel-link=\"external\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"external noopener noreferrer\">https://archive.is/SVI6R</a>"^^rdf:HTML .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/8617>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“The EPA was never intended to be our nation’s foremost environmental regulator. The states were to have regulatory primacy. That construct –a construct put in place by this body – has been turned upside down by this administration. That’s why I’m here today. I’d like to explain to you why I so jealously guard Oklahoma’s sovereign prerogative to regulate in both a sensible and sensitive way.”";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/8617/source/75>;
        schema:author            <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/entity/scott-pruitt/>;
        schema:claimInterpreter  <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:inLanguage        "English"^^schema:Text;
        schema:publisher         <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:url               "https://www.desmog.com/scott-pruitt/" .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/8616/source/74>
        rdf:type         schema:CreativeWork;
        schema:citation  "E. Scott Pruitt. <a href=\"http://web.archive.org/web/20161109222344/https://science.house.gov/sites/republicans.science.house.gov/files/documents/HHRG-114-SY18-WState-SPruitt-20160526.pdf\" data-wpel-link=\"external\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"external noopener noreferrer\">“Impact of the EPA’s Clean Power Plan on States” (PDF)</a>, <em>House Committee on Science, Space &amp; Technology</em>, May 26, 2016. Archived .pdf on file at DeSmog."^^rdf:HTML .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/8616>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“The EPA was never intended to be our nation’s foremost environmental regulator. The states were to have regulatory primacy. That construct –a construct put in place by this body – has been turned upside down by this administration. That’s why I’m here today. I’d like to explain to you why I so jealously guard Oklahoma’s sovereign prerogative to regulate in both a sensible and sensitive way.”";
