<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/8425>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“Teen school-skipping climate activists are testifying to the U.S. Congress and the United Nations and young children are being recruited for lawsuits against the U.S. government for its alleged climate ‘inaction.’ The phrase ‘climate emergency’ has emerged as the favorite for climate campaigners. But the arguments put forth by global warming advocates grossly distort the true facts on a host of issues, ranging from rising sea levels and record temperatures to melting polar caps and polar bears, among others. In short, there is no ‘climate crisis’ or a ‘climate emergency.’”";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/8425/source/88>;
        schema:author            <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/entity/marc-morano/>;
