<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/8372>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "”&nbsp;There’ve been studies recently, the last few years showing that mask wearing is associated with higher incidence of flu and influenza because you end up touching your mouth, more, adjusting it and getting the virus in. It’s it’s an amazing thing. But this is about obedience to government.”";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/8372/source/>;
