<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/8256>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "Quick interview after my debate with Andrew Dessler (of recent JRE fame) discussing why a Fossil Future is a great future and a fossil-free future is an unlivable future.";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/8256/source/>;
        schema:author            <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/entity/alex-epstein/>;
        schema:claimInterpreter  <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:inLanguage        "English"^^schema:Text;
        schema:publisher         <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:url               "https://www.desmog.com/alex-epstein/" .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/8255/source/>
        rdf:type         schema:CreativeWork;
        schema:citation  ""^^rdf:HTML .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/8255>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "He concluded: “They’re literally trying to destroy my life based on a hundred percent B.S. I mean, it’s even worse than B.S. because it’s really racist thinking that’s causing them to think, oh, praising Western culture is racist because Western culture is white, or criticizing a black icon is racist because you just can’t do that. Those are both racist ideas from my perspective. But in any case, I am not a racist. I’ve never been a racist. You are just being a total scumbag if you use this kind of tactic to call me racist and attack my work.”";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/8255/source/>;
        schema:author            <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/entity/alex-epstein/>;
        schema:claimInterpreter  <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:inLanguage        "English"^^schema:Text;
        schema:publisher         <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:url               "https://www.desmog.com/alex-epstein/" .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/8254/source/>
        rdf:type         schema:CreativeWork;
        schema:citation  ""^^rdf:HTML .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/8254>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“I do think Western culture is overall superior and certainly in terms of government historically, because it’s really the birth of modern freedom. But I do think there’s something valid in almost any culture. And you know, as I’ve gotten 22, 23 years older, that’s part of what you get. […] So it’s an obvious thing. There’s nothing here resembling racism,” he added.";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/8254/source/>;
        schema:author            <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/entity/alex-epstein/>;
        schema:claimInterpreter  <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:inLanguage        "English"^^schema:Text;
        schema:publisher         <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:url               "https://www.desmog.com/alex-epstein/" .

