<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/8122>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“As the atmospheric concentration of carbon increases, we are entering uncharted territory. Not since the dawn of humanity has there been anything like this. The models use the ‘best estimate’&nbsp;of impacts, but as we learn more about climate change these best estimates keep getting revised, and, typically, in only one direction — more damage and sooner than had been&nbsp;expected.”";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/8122/source/>;
        schema:author            <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/entity/bjorn-lomborg/>;
