<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/8121>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“A second mistake — which biases the results in the same way — is Nordhaus’s and Lomborg’s underestimation of the damage associated with climate change.” Examples of that damage&nbsp;include ocean acidification and sea level rise. “Climate change also includes more extreme weather events — more intense hurricanes, more droughts, more floods, with all the devastation to life, livelihood and property that accompanies&nbsp;them.”";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/8121/source/>;
