<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/7920/source/14>
        rdf:type         schema:CreativeWork;
        schema:citation  "“<a href=\"http://web.archive.org/web/20050525102006/www.theinterim.com/2005/apr/14qanda.html\" data-wpel-link=\"external\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"external noopener noreferrer\">Q <span class=\"amp\">&amp;</span> A with: Mark Crutcher</a>,” <em>The Interim</em>, April 2005. Archived May 25, 2005. Archive.is <span class=\"caps\">URL</span>: <a href=\"https://archive.is/eC9mH\" data-wpel-link=\"external\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"external noopener noreferrer\">https://archive.is/eC9mH</a>"^^rdf:HTML .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/7920>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“When I started Life Dynamics, one of the things I looked around for was what I perceived as holes in the (pro-life) effort. I had no interest in creating another pro-life organization to duplicate the efforts of the existing organizations. One of the things I noticed was that the pro-life movement had never developed a really sophisticated or professional counter-intelligence or intelligence-gathering mechanism. Everything we did on that front was somewhat haphazard and amateurish. That was something I knew something about&nbsp;…";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/7920/source/14>;
        schema:author            <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/entity/thirteen-foundation/>;
