<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/7784>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“How can this be AND the year also be the hottest on record! Simply put the correction algorithms used to compensate for the urban heat island effects are wrong. As are the majority if not all of the climate models used by the UN IPCC which do not take into account celestial cycles, cloud formation impacts of comic [sic] rays and numerous other parameters that are a bigger driver than CO2,” Leimkuhler wrote.";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/7784/source/6>;
