<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/7773>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "”[…] The reality is that atmospheric CO2 has a minimal impact on greenhouse gases and world temperature. Water vapor is responsible for 95 percent of the greenhouse effect. CO2 contributes just 3.6 percent, with human activity responsible for only 3.2 percent of that. That is why some studies claim CO2 levels are largely irrelevant to global warming.”";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/7773/source/13>;
