<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/7299>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“This week, Scholastic came under criticism for an 11” x 16” poster map which displays different sources of energy – coal, nuclear, hydroelectric, solar, wind and natural gas – not so much for the content of the poster but primarily for its sponsorship by the American Coal Foundation. We acknowledge that the mere fact of sponsorship may call into question the authenticity of the information, and therefore conclude that we were not vigilant enough as to the effect of sponsorship in this instance. We have no plans to further distribute this particular program.”";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/7299/source/>;
