<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/7269>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“To think we can do something is the ultimate of narcissism,” Plimer said. “And it’s all based on a failed fundamental: The fundamental is that it is the human emissions of carbon dioxide that drive global warming. That has never been shown. 99% of emissions are natural. “";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/7269/source/30>;
