        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“Should the nanny state regulate tobacco? No. Of course not,” Smith declared. He then went on to list out the supposed “threats these regulations pose to individual liberty,” while portraying smoking itself as a “symbol of freedom.” He also admits that “the hazards of smoking, we all know are real and they’re there.”";
