<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/7148/source/43>
        rdf:type         schema:CreativeWork;
        schema:citation  "“<a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=fqv83JrM58Q\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener nofollow external\" data-wpel-link=\"external\">Who is Department of Energy Nominee Chris Wright? | Real Talk</a>,” YouTube video uploaded by user “PragerU,” April 19, 2023. Archived .mp4 on file at DeSmog."^^rdf:HTML .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/7148>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“But to date, the changes are rather modest, rather slow moving. There’s almost as many positive changes. The planet’s getting greener and agricultural productivity is going up with more plant food in the air. There’s probably almost as many positive changes as there are negative changes. But that calculus probably changes with time. So it’s a very real issue dominantly caused by our industry. So real issue, yes. Is it a crisis? Is it the world’s greatest challenge or a big threat to the next generation? No.”";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/7148/source/43>;
        schema:author            <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/entity/chris-wright/>;
