<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/7064>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "CALLER: “Mr. Landry, as the Attorney General of the state that is suffering the most from climate change— I’m standing right now on Lower Plaquemines Parish—how do you justify your decision to support President Trump’s withdrawal from the Paris Climate Accord? Aren’t you telling the residents of this state, many of them in Republican areas, essentially ‘I don’t care if you drown’?”";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/7064/source/39>;
        schema:author            <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/entity/jeff-landry/>;
