        schema:citation  "“<a href=\"https://twitter.com/RepMikeJohnson/status/1630699590864207875\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener nofollow external\" data-wpel-link=\"external\">I was in the chair of the House Judiciary Committee today when Democrats argued for radical abortion policies &amp; insisted our rights are given to us by government instead of God. This was my response:</a>” post by user @RepMikeJohnson, February 28, 2023. Retrieved from twitter.com. Archived .mp4 on file at DeSmog."^^rdf:HTML .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/6891>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“We don’t have able bodied workers, enough of them in the economy to support our programs. Social Security and Medicare, for example. They’re all scheduled to go bankrupt in less than ten years, some of them. But why? Because we don’t have enough people paying into the system to support those programs. And why is that? Because 63 million of them were aborted,”";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/6891/source/61>;
