<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/6731>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“I hate the low carbon fuel standard. A low carbon fuel standard requires you to blend in gasoline a fuel that has a lower carbon intensity. Right now it’s ethanol. But as the standard ramps up, the low carbon fuel will be harder and harder to find. Because we haven’t cracked the nut. We can’t figure out what’s less carbon intensive than what we have. The minute you can’t get to the next increment — you’re going to pay more. The low carbon fuel standard is a regulation, and it’s not a regulation you can comply with.”";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/6731/source/19>;
        schema:author            <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/entity/western-states-petroleum-association/>;
