<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/6626>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“Scrapping clean power? Why, they must be in favor of dirtiness! But cleanliness has nothing to do with power in physics, which is simply energy per unit time. There is dirty power in play, but it does not come from physics. It comes from dirty politics: distorting language with false terms like ‘clean power’ to confuse and manipulate people. The objective is to befuddle minds into jumbling carbon dioxide together with soot and toxic gases, which are then cleansed with political virtue instead of engineering.";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/6626/source/13>;
        schema:author            <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/entity/christopher-essex/>;
