<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/6538>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“The IPCC consensus findings on attribution have been echoed in position statements made by many scientific organizations. The IPCC consensus is portrayed as nearly total among scientists with expertise and prominence in the field of climate science. The idea of a scientific consensus surrounding climate change attribution has been questioned by a number of people, including scientists and politicians. Much effort has been undertaken by those that support the IPCC consensus to discredit skeptical voices, essentially dismissing them as cranks or at best rebels, or even politically motivated ‘deniers’.";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/6538/source/>;
        schema:author            <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/entity/judith-curry/>;
        schema:claimInterpreter  <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:inLanguage        "English"^^schema:Text;
        schema:publisher         <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:url               "https://www.desmog.com/judith-curry/" .

