<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/6473>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“So how can Taylor make this claim? Well, as usual, it’s to cherry-pick a very, very specific set of circumstances: Satellite measurements of a single layer of the atmosphere. As I (and many others) have shown, these satellite measurements are not terribly reliable over the long term, and are nowhere near as accurate as temperatures measured from the ground using&nbsp;thermometers.";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/6473/source/51>;
        schema:author            <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/entity/james-taylor/>;
