<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/6339>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“The outcome of a Red/Blue exercise for climate science is not preordained, which makes such a process all the more valuable. It could reveal the current consensus as weaker than claimed. Alternatively, the consensus could emerge strengthened if Red Team criticisms were countered effectively. But whatever the outcome, we scientists would have better fulfilled our responsibilities to society, and climate policy discussions would be better informed,” Koonin ";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/6339/source/16>;
        schema:author            <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/entity/steve-koonin/>;
