<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/6286/source/53>
        rdf:type         schema:CreativeWork;
        schema:citation  "“<a href=\"http://www.hillheat.com/articles/2013/08/07/audio-rep-kevin-cramer-r-n-d-believes-global-warming-is-fraudulent-science-to-promote-wind-farms\" data-wpel-link=\"external\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"external noopener noreferrer\">AUDIO: Rep. Kevin Cramer (R-N.D.) Believes Global Warming Is ‘Fraudulent Science’ To Promote Wind Farms</a>,” <em>Hill Heat</em>, August 8, 2013. <a href=\"http://web.archive.org/web/20160525205900/http://www.hillheat.com/articles/2013/08/07/audio-rep-kevin-cramer-r-n-d-believes-global-warming-is-fraudulent-science-to-promote-wind-farms\" data-wpel-link=\"external\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"external noopener noreferrer\">Archived May 25, 2016</a>. WebCite URL: <a href=\"http://www.webcitation.org/6hmEh1l8H\" data-wpel-link=\"external\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"external noopener noreferrer\">http://www.webcitation.org/6hmEh1l8H</a>"^^rdf:HTML .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/6286>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“These mandates and these wind farms are all based on this fraudulent science from the EPA, meaning their claim that CO2 is a pollutant and is causing global warming. I’m sure you’re familiar with one of the leading climate research centers in the world there at East Anglia University in England, the Hadley Research Centre. The director, Phil Jones, his emails, he admitted that he was falsifying temperature data. The reason he had to do is because was the data was showing the global climate is actually declining in temperature, temperatures were going down. He was overlaying higher temperatures on the real data to show that it was actually rising. We know the globe is cooling. Number one, we know that. So the idea that CO2 is somehow causing global warming is on its face fraudulent.”";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/6286/source/53>;
        schema:author            <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/entity/kevin-cramer/>;
        schema:claimInterpreter  <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:inLanguage        "English"^^schema:Text;
        schema:publisher         <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:url               "https://www.desmog.com/kevin-cramer/" .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/6285/source/39>
        rdf:type         schema:CreativeWork;
        schema:citation  "Justin Mikulka. “<a href=\"//www.desmog.com/2014/09/08/how-many-crude-oil-scientists-will-testify-congressional-science-committee-hearing-bakken-crude-zero\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener external noreferrer\" data-wpel-link=\"external\">How Many Crude Oil Scientists Will Testify At Congressional Science Committee Hearing on Bakken Crude? Zero</a>,” DeSmog, September 8, 2014."^^rdf:HTML .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/6285>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“So for a hearing with the goal of determining the characteristics of Bakken crude oil, the experts include two firefighters, one oil industry lobbyist, a banker with oil industry experience and one engineer who just happens to work for the firm that issued the report saying Bakken is no different from other crude oils and does not require stabilization to make it safe for rail transport.”";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/6285/source/39>;
        schema:author            <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/entity/kevin-cramer/>;
        schema:claimInterpreter  <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:inLanguage        "English"^^schema:Text;
        schema:publisher         <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:url               "https://www.desmog.com/kevin-cramer/" .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/6284/source/38>
        rdf:type         schema:CreativeWork;
        schema:citation  "Justin Mikulka. “<a href=\"//www.desmog.com/2014/09/08/how-many-crude-oil-scientists-will-testify-congressional-science-committee-hearing-bakken-crude-zero\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener external noreferrer\" data-wpel-link=\"external\">How Many Crude Oil Scientists Will Testify At Congressional Science Committee Hearing on Bakken Crude? Zero</a>,” DeSmog, September 8, 2014."^^rdf:HTML .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/6284>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“I want three good solid scientists… consultants apart from all of the politicians and the presidential appointees. And I’ve promised them a very fair thorough review of the data and the evidence and the information. So that we can, you know, answer definitively and scientifically what is the volatility, if you will, of Bakken crude. How does it compare to other crudes?”";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/6284/source/38>;
        schema:author            <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/entity/kevin-cramer/>;
        schema:claimInterpreter  <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:inLanguage        "English"^^schema:Text;
        schema:publisher         <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:url               "https://www.desmog.com/kevin-cramer/" .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/6283/source/32>
        rdf:type         schema:CreativeWork;
        schema:citation  "Evan Lehmann. “<a href=\"http://www.eenews.net/stories/1060037208\" data-wpel-link=\"external\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"external noopener noreferrer\">CAMPAIGN 2016: Meet Donald Trump’s new energy adviser</a>,” E&amp;E Publishing, May 13, 2016. <a href=\"http://web.archive.org/web/20160525200806/http://www.eenews.net/stories/1060037208\" data-wpel-link=\"external\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"external noopener noreferrer\">Archived May 25, 2016</a>. WebCite URL: <a href=\"http://www.webcitation.org/6hmBMwh7c\" data-wpel-link=\"external\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"external noopener noreferrer\">http://www.webcitation.org/6hmBMwh7c</a>"^^rdf:HTML .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/6283>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“My idea of a carbon tax would be to help fund clean fossil fuel research and development, not to fund the government, not to punish fossil fuel generation, not to manipulate fuel choice,” Cramer said. “Even a neutral, a revenue-neutral, carbon tax is inappropriate, in my view. But if we can have a very, very modest carbon tax to fund, again, the solution by utilizing fossil fuels like coal, I think even the industry would support that.”";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/6283/source/32>;
        schema:author            <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/entity/kevin-cramer/>;
        schema:claimInterpreter  <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:inLanguage        "English"^^schema:Text;
        schema:publisher         <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:url               "https://www.desmog.com/kevin-cramer/" .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/6282/source/31>
        rdf:type         schema:CreativeWork;
        schema:citation  "Evan Lehmann. “<a href=\"http://www.eenews.net/stories/1060037208\" data-wpel-link=\"external\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"external noopener noreferrer\">CAMPAIGN 2016: Meet Donald Trump’s new energy adviser</a>,” E&amp;E Publishing, May 13, 2016. <a href=\"http://web.archive.org/web/20160525200806/http://www.eenews.net/stories/1060037208\" data-wpel-link=\"external\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"external noopener noreferrer\">Archived May 25, 2016</a>. WebCite URL: <a href=\"http://www.webcitation.org/6hmBMwh7c\" data-wpel-link=\"external\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"external noopener noreferrer\">http://www.webcitation.org/6hmBMwh7c</a>"^^rdf:HTML .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/6282>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“He can do all that if he wants,” Cramer said of Trump’s climate position. “But my advice would be, while I’m a skeptic, as well, he is a product of political populism, and political populism believes that there needs [to be] some addressing of climate change.”";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/6282/source/31>;
        schema:author            <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/entity/kevin-cramer/>;
        schema:claimInterpreter  <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:inLanguage        "English"^^schema:Text;
        schema:publisher         <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:url               "https://www.desmog.com/kevin-cramer/" .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/6281/source/24>
        rdf:type         schema:CreativeWork;
        schema:citation  "Justin Mikulka. “<a href=\"//www.desmog.com/2014/09/05/safety-citizens-bomb-train-blast-zones-hands-north-dakota-politicians\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener external noreferrer\" data-wpel-link=\"external\">Safety of Citizens in Bomb Train Blast Zones in Hands of North Dakota Politicians</a>,” <em>DeSmog</em>, September 5, 2014."^^rdf:HTML .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/6281>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“So scientifically can you do it? Sure, but you have to look at it holistically and consider all of the other elements including economics, and is the benefit of doing something like that does that trump other things like speed of trains, and what kind of cars.”";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/6281/source/24>;
        schema:author            <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/entity/kevin-cramer/>;
        schema:claimInterpreter  <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:inLanguage        "English"^^schema:Text;
        schema:publisher         <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:url               "https://www.desmog.com/kevin-cramer/" .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/6280/source/23>
        rdf:type         schema:CreativeWork;
        schema:citation  "“<a href=\"http://web.archive.org/web/20160525201326/https://cramer.house.gov/media-center/press-releases/cramer-joins-amicus-brief-to-overturn-epas-clean-power-plan\" data-wpel-link=\"external\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"external noopener noreferrer\">CRAMER JOINS AMICUS BRIEF TO OVERTURN EPA’S CLEAN POWER PLAN</a>,” Cramer.house.gov, February 23, 2016. Archived May 25, 2016. Full <a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/hk6cuja09yykamd/20160223AmicusBrief1.pdf?dl=0\" data-wpel-link=\"external\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"external noopener noreferrer\">Amicus Brief (.pdf)</a> on file at DeSmog. WebCite URL: <a href=\"http://www.webcitation.org/6hmBnIOX1\" data-wpel-link=\"external\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"external noopener noreferrer\">http://www.webcitation.org/6hmBnIOX1</a>"^^rdf:HTML .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/6280>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“The EPA’s actions are clearly illegal and violate the expressed intent of Congress,” Cramer said of the EPA’s Clean Power Plan. “In order to defend the law and authority of Congress I joined my colleagues to stand up to this Administration and oppose it’s actions in federal court. North Dakota’s electrical producers provide some of the most affordable electricity and maintain some of the cleanest air, but this Administration’s focus on implementing a radical environmental agenda threatens our economic future.”";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/6280/source/23>;
        schema:author            <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/entity/kevin-cramer/>;
