<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/6259>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“The challenge is not, ‘Either we believe in global warming and rescue the planet or we all die.’&nbsp;It is largely a choice between how much action to take now and how much in the future; and a choice between preventing or adapting to it. The science is still young. Some people take uncertainty as a reason to act, others take it as a reason to proceed slowly. Future generations will have the benefit of greater scientific knowledge, better technology, and greater wealth… . . The range of views expressed at our conference suggests that the debate is far from being over, and that there is still time for much-needed rational&nbsp;discussion.”";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/6259/source/29>;
        schema:author            <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/entity/american-institute-economic-research/>;
        schema:claimInterpreter  <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:inLanguage        "English"^^schema:Text;
        schema:publisher         <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:url               "https://www.desmog.com/american-institute-economic-research/" .

