        rdf:type         schema:CreativeWork;
        schema:citation  "Richard M. Ebeling. “<a href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20201010070224/https://www.aier.org/article/impeachment-at-home-and-climate-hysteria-abroad/\" data-wpel-link=\"external\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"external noopener noreferrer\">Impeachment at Home and Climate Hysteria Abroad,</a>” <em><span class=\"caps\">AIER</span></em>, October 1, 2019. Archived October 10, 2020. Archive <span class=\"caps\">URL</span>: <a href=\"https://archive.vn/mxxYB\" data-wpel-link=\"external\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"external noopener noreferrer\">https://archive.vn/mxxYB</a>"^^rdf:HTML .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/6226>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "Here we see another representation of politics in the 21st century, this time on the global stage. We see the constantly repeated naïve and arrogant turning to and presumption of ability by ‘government’&nbsp;to solve the problems of humanity, and in this case, a ‘problem’&nbsp;that is dubious about being a problem as serious as the proponents of global warming run around warning&nbsp;about.”";
