<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/6207/source/9>
        rdf:type         schema:CreativeWork;
        schema:citation  "Gene J. Koprowski. “<a href=\"http://www.foxnews.com/scitech/2009/12/18/czech-president-klaus-global-warming-science-new-religion/#ixzz1zxNzPNZ2\" data-wpel-link=\"external\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"external noopener noreferrer\">Czech President Klaus: Global Warming Not Science, but a ‘New Religion’</a>,” FoxNews.com, December 18, 2009."^^rdf:HTML .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/6207>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“I’m convinced that after years of studying the phenomenon, global warming is not the real issue of temperature. That is the issue of a new ideology or a new religion. A religion of climate change or a religion of global warming. This is a religion which tells us that the people are responsible for the current, very small increase in temperatures. And they should be punished.”";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/6207/source/9>;
        schema:author            <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/entity/vaclav-klaus/>;
        schema:claimInterpreter  <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:inLanguage        "English"^^schema:Text;
        schema:publisher         <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:url               "https://www.desmog.com/vaclav-klaus/" .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/6206/source/8>
        rdf:type         schema:CreativeWork;
        schema:citation  "Vaclav Klaus. “<a href=\"http://opinion.financialpost.com/2010/10/20/vaclav-klaus-an-anti-human-ideology/\" data-wpel-link=\"external\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"external noopener noreferrer\">Vaclav Klaus: An anti-human ideology</a>,” <em>Financial Post </em>(comment), October 20, 2010."^^rdf:HTML .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/6206>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“To reduce the interpretation of the causality of all kinds of climate changes and of global warming to one variable, CO2, or to a small proportion of one variable — human-induced CO2 — is impossible to accept. Elementary rationality and my decades-long experience with econometric modelling and statistical testing of scientific hypotheses tell me that it is impossible to make strong conclusions based on mere correlation of two (or more) time series.”";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/6206/source/8>;
        schema:author            <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/entity/vaclav-klaus/>;
        schema:claimInterpreter  <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:inLanguage        "English"^^schema:Text;
        schema:publisher         <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:url               "https://www.desmog.com/vaclav-klaus/" .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/6205/source/7>
        rdf:type         schema:CreativeWork;
        schema:citation  "“<a href=\"http://www.klaus.cz/clanky/266\" data-wpel-link=\"external\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"external noopener noreferrer\">The Other Side of Global Warming Alarmism</a>,” Václav Klaus, Chatham House, London, 7 November 2007. Retrieved from klaus.cz."^^rdf:HTML .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/6205>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“Nevertheless, there is another threat on the horizon. I see this threat in environmentalism which is becoming a new dominant ideology, if not a religion. Its main weapon is raising the alarm and predicting the human life endangering climate change based on man-made global warming… . It became politically correct to caricature us, who dare to speak about it, as those who are talking about things they do not understand and are not experts on. This criticism is inappropriate. People like me do not have ambitions to enter the field of climatology. They do not try to better measure global temperature or to present alternative scenarios of the future global climate fluctuations.”";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/6205/source/7>;
        schema:author            <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/entity/vaclav-klaus/>;
        schema:claimInterpreter  <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:inLanguage        "English"^^schema:Text;
        schema:publisher         <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:url               "https://www.desmog.com/vaclav-klaus/" .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/6204/source/>
        rdf:type         schema:CreativeWork;
        schema:citation  ""^^rdf:HTML .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/6204>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“… the climate change debate is basically not about science; it is about ideology. It is not about global temperature; it is about the concept of human society. It is not about scientific ecology; it is about environmentalism, which is a new anti-individualistic, pseudo-collectivistic ideology based on putting nature and environment and their supposed protection and preservation before and above freedom.”";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/6204/source/>;
        schema:author            <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/entity/vaclav-klaus/>;
        schema:claimInterpreter  <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:inLanguage        "English"^^schema:Text;
        schema:publisher         <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:url               "https://www.desmog.com/vaclav-klaus/" .

