        schema:citation  "“<a href=\"http://web.archive.org/web/20170713182820/https://wattsupwiththat.com/2017/06/14/wuwt-at-10-years-i-need-some-help-please/\" rel=\"nofollow external noopener noreferrer\" data-wpel-link=\"external\" target=\"_blank\">WUWT at 10+ years – I need some help, please</a>,” <em>Watts Up With That?</em>, June 14, 2017. Archived July 13, 2017. Archive.is URL: <a href=\"https://archive.is/WZ9RH\" data-wpel-link=\"external\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"external noopener noreferrer\">https://archive.is/WZ9RH</a>"^^rdf:HTML .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/6130>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“Here is what I want to do: Take a month off. Disconnect. Then come back fresh. […] To do that though, and keep WUWT running, requires help. […] I’m asking for two things: help with content/moderating, and some donations, so that I can choose a place to go disconnect, and not worry. I don’t want a staycation, and if that darned Koch Brothers check that many Mann-like people seem to think I’m getting would just show up in the mailbox, I’d not have to ask.”";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/6130/source/76>;
        schema:author            <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/entity/anthony-watts/>;
        schema:claimInterpreter  <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:inLanguage        "English"^^schema:Text;
        schema:publisher         <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:url               "https://www.desmog.com/anthony-watts/" .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/6129/source/79>
        rdf:type         schema:CreativeWork;
        schema:citation  "“<a href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20170119211552/http://cornwallalliance.org/landmark-documents/open-letter-supporting-scott-pruitt-for-epa-administrator/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener external noreferrer\" data-wpel-link=\"external\">Open Letter Supporting Scott Pruitt for EPA Administrator</a>,” <em>Cornwall Alliance</em>, January 5, 2017. Archived January 19, 2017. Archive.is URL: <a href=\"https://archive.is/xMash\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener external noreferrer\" data-wpel-link=\"external\">https://archive.is/xMash</a>"^^rdf:HTML .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/6129>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“Mr. Pruitt has also demonstrated understanding of and open-mindedness toward scientific insights crucial to the formulation and implementation of environmental regulation. He is prepared to hear all sides in debates over the risks and benefits of various activities that come under the purview of the EPA,” reads the letter.";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/6129/source/79>;
        schema:author            <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/entity/anthony-watts/>;
        schema:claimInterpreter  <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:inLanguage        "English"^^schema:Text;
        schema:publisher         <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:url               "https://www.desmog.com/anthony-watts/" .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/6128/source/>
        rdf:type         schema:CreativeWork;
        schema:citation  ""^^rdf:HTML .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/6128>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“During his tenure as Attorney General of Oklahoma, Mr. Pruitt has blurred the distinction between official and political actions, often at the behest of corporations he will regulate if confirmed to lead EPA,” the letter said. “Public reporting based on documents produced by Freedom of Information Act requests illustrate how Mr. Pruitt and members of his staff have worked closely with fossil fuel lobbyists to craft his office’s official positions.”";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/6128/source/>;
        schema:author            <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/entity/anthony-watts/>;
        schema:claimInterpreter  <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:inLanguage        "English"^^schema:Text;
        schema:publisher         <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:url               "https://www.desmog.com/anthony-watts/" .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/6127/source/86>
        rdf:type         schema:CreativeWork;
        schema:citation  "E. Calvin Beisner. “<a href=\"http://web.archive.org/web/20160624193309/http://cornwallalliance.org/2016/06/open-letter-to-attorneys-general-about-climate-change/\" data-wpel-link=\"external\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"external noopener noreferrer\">Open Letter to Attorneys General about Climate Change</a>,” Cornwall Alliance, June 10, 2016. Archived June 24, 2016. Archive.is URL: <a href=\"https://archive.is/SjRkt\" data-wpel-link=\"external\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"external noopener noreferrer\">https://archive.is/SjRkt</a>"^^rdf:HTML .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/6127>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“[U]nlike in the case of tobacco’s health risks, there are innumerable and enormous holes in the case (not for human contribution to global warming but) for manmade global warming dangerous enough to justify spending trillions of dollars reinventing the world’s energy system to mitigate it, particularly when competing use of those trillions might bring far greater benefit,” Beisner addresses the attorneys general. And you, intelligent and learned all, are ignorant of those enormous holes.”";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/6127/source/86>;
        schema:author            <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/entity/anthony-watts/>;
