<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/5603>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "In his opening statement, Happer admits “I am not a climatologist, but I don’t think any of the other witnesses are either.” He then goes on to state that “I believe that the increase of CO2 is not a cause for alarm and will be good for mankind,” comparing policies designed to reduce emissions to the U.S. prohibition of alcohol.";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/5603/source/>;
        schema:author            <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/entity/george-c-marshall-institute/>;
