<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/5478>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“Alberta is a cold place blessed with huge coal, oil, and gas resources. Regarding ‘global warming,’ Albertans are inordinately skeptical. Despite this, the Government of Alberta is so concerned with ‘global warming’ it spends $500 million a year assailing this phantom menace. […] Environmentalists claim wilderness parks preserve Alberta’s ‘natural heritage.’ In reality, Alberta’s environment has undergone so many natural transformations that any talk of preservation betrays an ahistorical, unscientific mindset.”";
