<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/5336>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“Those donations from the late 1990s and early 2000s reflect the perspective of our leadership at the time that overzealous&nbsp;environmental regulation, premised on climate change, would be harmful for economic growth in general, and especially for the opportunity to increase living standards in the Global South. Certainly, many free-market think tanks continue to agree with this thinking. However, by the time I became CEO of Atlas Network fifteen years ago [2009], it was clear that there was little&nbsp;consensus on these topics among our partners. I determined this should not be an area of focus for Atlas Network, as we want to work constructively with all our partners on our key priorities with no concern for where they land on questions of climate science.”";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/5336/source/6>;
