<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/5299/source/46>
        rdf:type         schema:CreativeWork;
        schema:citation  "“<a href=\"https://www.dailykos.com/stories/2020/5/20/1946378/-While-Greta-Set-Up-a-Foundation-Anti-Greta-Naomi-Seibt-Gets-Fined-Starts-Patreon\" data-wpel-link=\"external\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"external noopener noreferrer\">While Greta Set Up a Foundation, Anti-Greta Naomi Seibt Gets Fined, Starts Patreon</a>,” <em>Daily KOS</em>, May 20, 2020. <a href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20200529210947/https://www.dailykos.com/stories/2020/5/20/1946378/-While-Greta-Set-Up-a-Foundation-Anti-Greta-Naomi-Seibt-Gets-Fined-Starts-Patreon\" data-wpel-link=\"external\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"external noopener noreferrer\">Archived May 29, 2020</a>. Archive URL: <a href=\"https://archive.vn/Z8hnB\" data-wpel-link=\"external\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"external noopener noreferrer\">https://archive.vn/Z8hnB</a>"^^rdf:HTML .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/5299>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“Given that he doesn’t provide links to any of the original materials, it’s hard to tell the difference between the dramatic hyperbole of Monckton’s writing — which is basically how an arrogant and lazy British person thinks a witty and brilliant British professor-turned-thesaurus-salesman talked in 1820 — and what’s actually happened here in 2020. But it sounds like the German state in which Seibt lives has a new law regulating media that lobbies for or against specific policies, and that includes some sort of product placement, which her videos apparently do.”";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/5299/source/46>;
