<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/5296>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“Coming out can still be a very tough thing to do. However, I’m not talking about coming out as gay, but coming out as non-leftist, coming out as conservative, or libertarian even. Coming out as a voter for a specific party, or a supporter of particular people in the political sphere. Coming out as a severe critic of the migration crisis, the welfare state, or coming out as a climate change skeptic. People like us tend to be shunned as evil and heartless immediately. …”";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/5296/source/29>;
        schema:author            <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/entity/naomi-seibt/>;
        schema:claimInterpreter  <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:inLanguage        "English"^^schema:Text;
        schema:publisher         <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:url               "https://www.desmog.com/naomi-seibt/" .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/5295/source/28>
        rdf:type         schema:CreativeWork;
        schema:citation  "“<a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=I2lkJeSkEtg\" rel=\"nofollow external noopener noreferrer\" data-wpel-link=\"external\" target=\"_blank\">Watch: The un-Greta teen activist: Climate skeptic teen Naomi Seibt: ‘Greta is stuck in a bubble’</a>,” <em>Climate Depot</em>, December 16, 2019. Archived .mp4 on file at DeSmog."^^rdf:HTML .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/5295>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“The reason I don’t like the term ‘anti-Greta’ is because it suggests that I myself am an indoctrinated puppet, I guess, for the other side.”";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/5295/source/28>;
