<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/5267>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "The remarks were part of a video discussion that appears to have been deleted. They were seen by some experts as saying that Germans had less pity for “ordinary German” victims of crime than for Jews and Muslims. A portion of the discussion was included in a report by ZDF and is still available online,”&nbsp;Stephanie Kirchgaessner and Emily Holden reported at&nbsp;";
