<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/5153>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“You can’t have reliable electricity, affordable, reliable electricity, without baseload generation,” Wheeler said. “What the Sierra Club proposes for wind and solar, that’s not baseload. We don’t have the battery capacity yet to deliver solar and wind as baseload generation. You end up having middle-income, lower-income families with electricity rates wildly&nbsp;variable.”";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/5153/source/49>;
