<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/5002>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“But if developing countries are going to prepare for possible changes in the climate, they will have to get richer so they can afford to deal with any calamities that may occur. And how will they get richer? The answer is obvious: by consuming more energy. And for countries throughout the developing world, the lowest-cost energy is still coal,” Bryce writes.";
