<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/4896>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“Given that he doesn’t provide links to any of the original materials, it’s hard to tell the difference between the dramatic hyperbole of Monckton’s writing – which is basically how an arrogant and lazy British person thinks a witty and brilliant British professor-turned-thesaurus-salesman talked in 1820 – and what’s actually happened here in 2020. But it sounds like the German state in which Seibt lives has a new law regulating media that lobbies for or against specific policies, and that includes some sort of product placement, which her videos apparently do.”";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/4896/source/57>;
