<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/4684>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“In reality, the Paris agreement was no more than a vainglorious act of collective wishful thinking, orchestrated to fool the world into thinking that anything of significance had actually been achieved,” Brooker Writes. “For the rest of us, of course, the one huge consolation from all this is that nothing said or done in Paris will have the slightest effect on the world’s climate – as eventually, to their undying shame if they live long enough, all those poor deluded politicians may come to realise.”";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/4684/source/42>;
