<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/4430>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“Although the campaign was successful in some ways—it had gained respectful, if not plentiful, media attention, inspired some 300 Students for Clark organizations, distributed hundreds of thousands of copies of its campaign book, and placed no less than 47 five-minute ads on national television—the results were disappointing. Following the 1980 campaign, many of Clark’s key supporters appear to have lost interest in the party, and a number of them drifted away.”";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/4430/source/>;
