<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/4397>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "TASSC members believe that science that is used to guide public policy decisions should be based on sound principles – not on emotions or beliefs considered by some as politically acceptable. Too often, public policy decisions that are based on inadequate science impose enormous economic costs and other hardships on consumers, businesses and government. Furthermore, these decisions may fail to protect the public’s health and safety.";
