<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/4391>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“We must be able to use our own natural gas supplies, which are right under our feet as well as out to sea. Using our own gas will bring investment, jobs, a good helping of taxes and reduce emissions compared to imported gas, which often comes with geopolitical strings attached. To say that we ought not to try because it might not make that much of a difference to prices is utterly defeatist, neglecting the experience of the USA. It’s for businesses to experiment in the marketplace and not for the government to arbitrarily cancel industries and manage prices based on a hunch that may prove to be wrong.”";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/4391/source/>;
        schema:author            <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/entity/craig-mackinlay/>;
