<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/4251/source/17>
        rdf:type         schema:CreativeWork;
        schema:citation  "Leo Hickman. “<a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/environment/blog/2009/nov/30/douglas-carswell-climate-change\" data-wpel-link=\"external\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"external noopener noreferrer\">Douglas Carswell: How the facts on global warming have changed</a>,”<em> The Guardian</em>, November 30, 2009. <a href=\"http://web.archive.org/web/20200221184943/https://www.theguardian.com/environment/blog/2009/nov/30/douglas-carswell-climate-change\" data-wpel-link=\"external\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"external noopener noreferrer\">Archived January 5, 2021</a>. Archive.vn URL: <a href=\"https://archive.vn/EOp1q\" data-wpel-link=\"external\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"external noopener noreferrer\">https://archive.vn/EOp1q</a>"^^rdf:HTML .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/4251>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“I suspect what will happen is people will become more aware of the fact that the public is being expected to pay ever more for public policy solutions on climate change and I think the consensus about this will begin to shift and I suspect it’s beginning to happen already actually. I recently listened to a debate on Radio 4 and the counter arguments were being put. I think there’s going to come a correction in the market for ideas and I suspect that in a few years’ time there will be more doubts about man-made climate change.”";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/4251/source/17>;
        schema:author            <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/entity/douglas-carswell/>;
