<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/4247>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“One thing hasn’t changed and won’t change: Catastrophizing climate change for political ends,” Darwall wrote. “It’s hard to escape the conclusion that the inability to distinguish between a genuine crisis and an imagined one in the midst of the worst pandemic in a century is a manifestation of a collective psychological disorder.”";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/4247/source/54>;
