<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/4125>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "By way of comparison, the toll from the flu in the United States since October ran as follows: between 36 to 51 million infections, between 370 thousand to 670 thousand flu hospitalizations, and between 22 thousand to 55 thousand flu deaths. That works out to between roughly between 230,000 to 320,000 new infections per day, and between 140 to 350 deaths per day for an overall mortality rate of between 0.044 percent to 0.152&nbsp;percent.”";
