<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/4122>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“Because rich economies sequester more carbon than poor ones, stored carbon must be subtracted from emissions to determine an economy’s net addition to greenhouse gas emissions. McCormick’s data show that ‘rich countries take more carbon out of the air than poorer ones’ and that ‘the growth rate of net carbon emission per person will soon be negative in the United States.’ Put differently—richer may well be cooler.”";
