<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/3935>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“The most burdensome Obama-era regulation is the Clean Power Plan” Smith said. “The EPA’s sweeping climate change regulations burden the entire U.S. economy, targeted our energy development, and threatened to abolish affordable electricity for all Americans. […] it was all pain and no gain.”";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/3935/source/>;
        schema:author            <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/entity/lamar-smith/>;
