<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/3900>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“The House Committee on Science, Space, and Technology (the Committee) is troubled by the Security and Exchange Commission’s (SEC) recently announced investigation of Exxon Mobil Corporation (Exxon)” the letter reads. “It appears from press accounts that the SEC’s investigative actions, which date back to at least August of this year, are couched in concerns related to the science of climate change. […] the AG’s efforts, characterized variously as a ‘witch hunt’ and ‘fool’s errand,’ an ‘abuse of powers,’ ‘pathetic,’ a ‘schtick,’ 7 and an ‘uphill battle,’ have failed to uncover any indicia of wrongdoing by Exxon. This raises questions as to why the SEC would assume the mantle of the New York AG’s fruitless investigation.”";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/3900/source/101>;
        schema:author            <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/entity/lamar-smith/>;
        schema:claimInterpreter  <http://desmog.com/>;
