<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/3752/source/45>
        rdf:type         schema:CreativeWork;
        schema:citation  "(Press Release). “<a href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20081006040020/http://royalsociety.org/news.asp?id=7901\" data-wpel-link=\"external\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"external noopener noreferrer\">Royal Society response to OFCOM decision on ’The Great Global Warming Swindle’</a>,” <em>The Royal Society</em>, July 21, 2008. Archived October 6, 2008. Archive URL: <a href=\"https://archive.ph/f9Y3Z\" data-wpel-link=\"external\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"external noopener noreferrer\">https://archive.ph/f9Y3Z</a>"^^rdf:HTML .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/3752>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“TV companies occasionally commission programmes just to court controversy, but to misrepresent the evidence on an issue as important as global warming was surely irresponsible. ‘The Great Global Warming Swindle’ was itself a swindle. The programme makers misrepresented the science, the views of some of the scientists featured in the programme and the work of the Intergovernmental Panel on Climate Change,” Rees ";
