<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/3736>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "Climate change has happened and will happen, pollution too has happened naturally in the two biggest volcanisms in Earth history in Siberia at Permian -Triassic boundary in Siberia and later at K-T boundary in India represented by our globally famous Deccan Volcanics. Life nearly disappeared at P-T boundary &amp; later Dinosaurs had to say adieu around 65 million years ago because of volcanic pollution not at all of their making.";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/3736/source/7>;
