<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/3725>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "Earth was quite beautiful before man and it will be quite beautiful after man. Moment of truth is before us. How long we delay our departure, is the question. We owe it to our next generations and the biodiversity we share the planet with, to learn from geological history: pollution wipes out even dinosaurs who spanned over 155 million years. We just arrived, let us stay a bit”";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/3725/source/7>;
