<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/3724>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "But the pollution by man may be petty from Geological history view point though, yet it can be fatal for humans if our lungs, livers, kidneys, joints and skins are already decaying and degenerating due the toxins we are inhaling day in and day out. Infants and oldies will go first but others too shall follow. Choice is tough but has to be made. Now or never are the options. Climate change is always a long term issue but skyline change is not even a short term issue but an existing disaster unforeseen.";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/3724/source/7>;
