        rdf:type         schema:CreativeWork;
        schema:citation  "“<a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=uA7OdRLaicg\" rel=\"nofollow external noopener noreferrer\" data-wpel-link=\"external\" target=\"_blank\">Amanda Maxham on Panel 3: Why CO2 Emissions Are Not Creating a Climate Crisis</a>,” YouTube video uploaded by user “The Heartland Institute,” August 13, 2018. Archived .mp4 on file at DeSmog."^^rdf:HTML .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/3676>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "[12:55] “The greenhouse effect is real, and we need to consider carefully what affect the carbon dioxide has on our atmosphere because we care about individual human beings. About their prosperity and their safety. If it turned out that mankind was destroying our ability to thrive by burning fossil fuels, that would be a horrible tragedy. I don’t think that’s the case, but we need to think about the question and examine it for ourselves.”";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/3676/source/9>;
        schema:author            <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/entity/amanda-maxham/>;
