<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/3659>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "Low number of used for reconstruction subfossil series is explained by standardisation method (“corridor method”). We had to select the longest series. The same concerns to living trees. There are not much old living trees in this area (in contrast to Polar Urals), therefore we used only 17 (not 12) samples from living trees. At that time we had close collaboration with CRU and I sent to Keith Briffa these raw data.";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/3659/source/71>;
