<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/3246/source/>
        rdf:type         schema:CreativeWork;
        schema:citation  ""^^rdf:HTML .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/3246>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“…successive governments, egged on by the CCC, the renewables industry, and the green movement have told us we must “keep fossil fuels in the ground”. […] So we first made the electricity grid unwelcoming for gas-fired power stations, then we neutered the nascent shale gas industry with absurd regulations, and then we banned it completely.”";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/3246/source/>;
        schema:author            <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/entity/steve-baker/>;
        schema:claimInterpreter  <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:inLanguage        "English"^^schema:Text;
        schema:publisher         <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:url               "https://www.desmog.com/steve-baker/" .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/3245/source/>
        rdf:type         schema:CreativeWork;
        schema:citation  ""^^rdf:HTML .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/3245>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“That does include actually growing food as a thing that we do in the UK. And I’m afraid some of the policies which are being adopted are just anti-life. They’re anti-human life on Earth in the name of environmentalism, and I want us to live flourishing and full lives with a healthy environment around us.”";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/3245/source/>;
        schema:author            <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/entity/steve-baker/>;
        schema:claimInterpreter  <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:inLanguage        "English"^^schema:Text;
        schema:publisher         <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:url               "https://www.desmog.com/steve-baker/" .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/3244/source/>
        rdf:type         schema:CreativeWork;
        schema:citation  ""^^rdf:HTML .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/3244>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“Climate science does appear to be subject to uncertainties and climate change appears to be a problem we face in the medium to long term. But I remember the fuel protests. I lived in a remote Cotswold hamlet and I came close to running out of food as well as fuel. I remember the queues and the anxiety and how quickly the situation developed. I remember thinking that we were only ever a couple of meals from barbarism. Perhaps resource depletion is a greater threat than climate change.”";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/3244/source/>;
        schema:author            <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/entity/steve-baker/>;
        schema:claimInterpreter  <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:inLanguage        "English"^^schema:Text;
        schema:publisher         <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:url               "https://www.desmog.com/steve-baker/" .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/3243/source/>
        rdf:type         schema:CreativeWork;
        schema:citation  ""^^rdf:HTML .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/3243>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“[B]ad economic science is a greater threat to civilisation than climate change.”";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/3243/source/>;
        schema:author            <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/entity/steve-baker/>;
        schema:claimInterpreter  <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:inLanguage        "English"^^schema:Text;
        schema:publisher         <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:url               "https://www.desmog.com/steve-baker/" .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/3242/source/38>
        rdf:type         schema:CreativeWork;
        schema:citation  "Simon Evans. “<a href=\"https://twitter.com/DrSimEvans/status/1425688765096464385\" data-wpel-link=\"external\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"external noopener noreferrer\">Factcheck: False. The @theCCCuk balanced net-zero pathway involves a 20% reduction in meat &amp; dairy by 2030 – continuing the trajectory of recent trends. It makes no mention of “gross insects”. (And other pathways to net-zero are available)</a>,” Tweet by @DrSimEvans, August 12, 2021. Retrieved from Twitter.com. Archived .png on file at DeSmog."^^rdf:HTML .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/3242>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“Factcheck: False. The @theCCCuk balanced net-zero pathway involves a 20% reduction in meat &amp; dairy by 2030 – continuing the trajectory of recent trends. It makes no mention of “gross insects”. (And other pathways to net-zero are available)”";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/3242/source/38>;
