<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/3062/source/22>
        rdf:type         schema:CreativeWork;
        schema:citation  "<a id=\"s21\" href=\"http://web.archive.org/web/20160804173707/http://clexit.net/wp-content/uploads/2016/07/clexit.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener external noreferrer\" name=\"s21\" data-wpel-link=\"external\">“After Brexit, Clexit” (PDF)</a>, <em>Clexit.net</em>. Archived .pdf on file at Desmog."^^rdf:HTML .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/3062>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“If the Paris climate accord is ratified, or enforced locally by compliant governments, it will strangle the leading economies of the world with pointless carbon taxes and costly climate and energy policies, all with no sound basis in evidence or science […]”";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/3062/source/22>;
        schema:author            <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/entity/hans-hj-labohm/>;
        schema:claimInterpreter  <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:inLanguage        "English"^^schema:Text;
        schema:publisher         <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:url               "https://www.desmog.com/hans-hj-labohm/" .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/3061/source/13>
        rdf:type         schema:CreativeWork;
        schema:citation  "Hans H.J. Labohm. “<a href=\"http://web.archive.org/web/20110701091857/http://www.ideasinactiontv.com/tcs_daily/2007/11/proliferation-of-climate-scepticism-in-europe.html\" data-wpel-link=\"external\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"external noopener noreferrer\">Proliferation of Climate Scepticism in Europe</a>,” <em>TCS Daily</em>, November 5, 2007. Archived July 1, 2011."^^rdf:HTML .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/3061>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“Nevertheless, in my capacity as expert reviewer of the IPCC, I have also received (a tiny) part of the Nobel price, which has been awarded to Al Gore and the IPCC (yes, thanks for your congratulations). Should I be grateful? I don’t think so. Both ‘An Inconvenient Truth’ and the latest IPCC report labour under cherry-picking, spindoctoring and scare-mongering (Al Gore’s movie more than the IPCC reports). Awarding the Nobel price for such flawed science is a disgrace.”";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/3061/source/13>;
        schema:author            <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/entity/hans-hj-labohm/>;
        schema:claimInterpreter  <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:inLanguage        "English"^^schema:Text;
        schema:publisher         <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:url               "https://www.desmog.com/hans-hj-labohm/" .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/3060/source/>
        rdf:type         schema:CreativeWork;
        schema:citation  ""^^rdf:HTML .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/3060>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“As far as the polar bears ears are concerned, polar bears has survived many periods of climate change over the last two, three, four, 5,000 years in the past. And at the moment, the polar bear population is thriving. The number of polar bears has grown dramatically over the last 50 years. Estimates range from a factor two to effect of five. So there’s nothing wrong with the polar bears.”";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/3060/source/>;
        schema:author            <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/entity/hans-hj-labohm/>;
        schema:claimInterpreter  <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:inLanguage        "English"^^schema:Text;
        schema:publisher         <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:url               "https://www.desmog.com/hans-hj-labohm/" .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/3059/source/12>
        rdf:type         schema:CreativeWork;
        schema:citation  "“<a href=\"http://web.archive.org/web/20191029025810/http://climaterealists.com/?id=2062\" data-wpel-link=\"external\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"external noopener noreferrer\">Video: Climate Change. Interview with Hans Labohm</a>,” <em>Climate Realists, </em>November 8, 2008. Full video archived at DeSmog."^^rdf:HTML .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/3059>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“For Al Gore and others to suggest that there are many horrible things going on in the world and attributes it to man-made global warming but there is no convincing scientific evidence to substantiate those claims. Consequently, his assertions are pure fiction, not even science fiction.”";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/3059/source/12>;
        schema:author            <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/entity/hans-hj-labohm/>;
