<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/2907>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“A final concern related to the ongoing rise in the air’s CO2 concentration is the worry that it may lead to catastrophic global warming. There is little reason to believe that such will ever occur, however, for several observations of historical changes in atmospheric CO2 concentration and air temperature suggest that it is climate change that drives changes in the air’s CO2 content and not vice versa.”";
