        schema:abstract          "“[W]hen there are fewer ions, the clouds that are formed are composed of large drops. Clouds of this type are less white and refract less of the sun’s rays outward, and so the heat is preserved and the earth gets warmer,” Shaviv says.";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/2624/source/11>;
        schema:author            <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/entity/nir-shaviv/>;
