<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/2244>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“Tom Nelson has an MS degree in Electrical and Electronics Engineering. He was involved in tech and software for many years. In 2005, as an avid bird-watcher, he became heavily involved in debunking a high-profile, but bogus ‘Ivory-billed Woodpecker’ rediscovery that opened his eyes to the problems with blindly trusting ‘peer-reviewed science’. Then a meteorologist pointed out lots of parallels between that woodpecker debate and the climate change debate, and Tom has been debunking climate change claims online almost daily since then.”";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/2244/source/7>;
        schema:author            <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/entity/tom-nelson/>;
        schema:claimInterpreter  <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:inLanguage        "English"^^schema:Text;
        schema:publisher         <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:url               "https://www.desmog.com/tom-nelson/" .

