<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/1965>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“The effect of solar winds on cosmic radiation has just recently been established and, furthermore, there seems to be a good correlation between cloudiness and variations in the intensity of cosmic radiation. Here we have a mechanism which is a far better explanation to variations in global climate than the attempts by IPCC to blame it all on anthropogenic input of greenhouse gases.”";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/1965/source/8>;
