<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/1915>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“There might be some adverse outcomes from that eight tenths of a degree of temperature rise threatening my Grandchildren in 2050, but neither I nor anyone else knows what those outcomes might be. We’ll assuredly get an extra flood over here, and one less flood over there, it’s very likely to be drier somewhere and wetter somewhere else, in other words, the climate will do what climate has done since forever — change.”";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/1915/source/9>;
