<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/1749>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "But like the Paris climate accord, there is a national security implication here. What we were doing for years is bringing oil from Canada, a reliable partner at a very good price, bringing their oil down to Texas for refining. Now, without the Keystone Pipeline, Canada is going to look for alternatives. They’ll probably send it west to their own ports and send it to China for refining, something I mentioned earlier. Or they’ll send it outside on the world market.";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/1749/source/>;
        schema:author            <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/entity/one-america-news-network-oann/>;
        schema:claimInterpreter  <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:inLanguage        "English"^^schema:Text;
        schema:publisher         <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:url               "https://www.desmog.com/one-america-news-network-oann/" .

