<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/1604>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“Whether or not we meet our targets for emissions reductions is of far less consequence, to the world or ourselves, than whether we cripple our economy in the process. That’s by no means inevitable. It depends on how we go about it: on the policy choices we make. Specifically, it depends on whether we rely on prices, in the main, to bring about the needed reductions, or whether we use subsidies and regulations to get there.";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/1604/source/>;
