<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/1576>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“‘The relevant facts in Kenya don’t support these claims,’ Beisner said. And to support his rebuttal, he presented data from a World Bank website indicating that for Kenya as a whole, neither average monthly temperature nor rainfall had changed materially over the last century. ‘Are poor Kenyans suffering from water shortages?’ asked Beisner. ‘Yes. Is that because of global warming—manmade or natural? No. Is fighting global warming the solution? No.’";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/1576/source/>;
