<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/1327>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“In several cases, the coalition agenda is sprawling and the distinguishing features aren’t immediately evident. Four broad themes are at work. Each constitutes some kind of threat to investment intentions, the health of rural communities, and a successful economy that benefits all British Columbia residents:";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/1327/source/>;
        schema:author            <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/entity/stewart-muir/>;
        schema:claimInterpreter  <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:inLanguage        "English"^^schema:Text;
        schema:publisher         <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:url               "https://www.desmog.com/stewart-muir/" .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/1326/source/>
        rdf:type         schema:CreativeWork;
        schema:citation  ""^^rdf:HTML .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/1326>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“Capital formation for innovation and decarbonization requires real commercial viability and an enabling regulatory regime. Why would anyone ever invest in building these (speculative) things in Canada when we can’t even get the existing goods to market? Why invest in Canada’s energy future, when we can’t even project confidence on the present opportunities?”";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/1326/source/>;
        schema:author            <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/entity/stewart-muir/>;
        schema:claimInterpreter  <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:inLanguage        "English"^^schema:Text;
        schema:publisher         <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:url               "https://www.desmog.com/stewart-muir/" .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/1325/source/>
        rdf:type         schema:CreativeWork;
        schema:citation  ""^^rdf:HTML .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/1325>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“Alberta’s energy patch is leaner today, with a renewed determination to succeed in the new, low-emissions world. Oil companies are going into the carbon-management business. Not just companies but also governments, small business owners, workers and First Nations with their own economic aspirations are seeing the writing on the wall: only with greatly improved environmental performance can this story continue,” they wrote.";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/1325/source/>;
        schema:author            <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/entity/stewart-muir/>;
        schema:claimInterpreter  <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:inLanguage        "English"^^schema:Text;
        schema:publisher         <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:url               "https://www.desmog.com/stewart-muir/" .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/1324/source/24>
        rdf:type         schema:CreativeWork;
        schema:citation  "Stewart Muir.”<a href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20221207205921/https://www.theglobeandmail.com/business/commentary/article-look-to-venezuela-for-why-albertas-canadian-energy-war-room-is/\" rel=\"nofollow external noopener noreferrer\" data-wpel-link=\"external\" target=\"_blank\">Look to Venezuela for why Alberta’s Canadian energy ‘war room’ is needed</a>,” <em>The Globe and Mail</em>, May 1, 2019. Archived December 7, 2022. Archive URL: <a href=\"https://archive.ph/QElWW\" data-wpel-link=\"external\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"external noopener noreferrer\">https://archive.ph/QElWW</a>"^^rdf:HTML .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/1324>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“Too many people fail to appreciate Canada represents the good guys in the international oil business. Our product is ethical, our workers are well treated, law and environmental rules followed, and Canadian families benefit directly from oil sales. Too few of the world’s top oil exporters can say the same, and certainly not Saudi Arabia, Iran, Iraq, Russia or Venezuela.”";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/1324/source/24>;
        schema:author            <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/entity/stewart-muir/>;
        schema:claimInterpreter  <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:inLanguage        "English"^^schema:Text;
        schema:publisher         <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:url               "https://www.desmog.com/stewart-muir/" .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/1323/source/24>
        rdf:type         schema:CreativeWork;
        schema:citation  "Stewart Muir.”<a href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20221207205921/https://www.theglobeandmail.com/business/commentary/article-look-to-venezuela-for-why-albertas-canadian-energy-war-room-is/\" rel=\"nofollow external noopener noreferrer\" data-wpel-link=\"external\" target=\"_blank\">Look to Venezuela for why Alberta’s Canadian energy ‘war room’ is needed</a>,” <em>The Globe and Mail</em>, May 1, 2019. Archived December 7, 2022. Archive URL: <a href=\"https://archive.ph/QElWW\" data-wpel-link=\"external\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"external noopener noreferrer\">https://archive.ph/QElWW</a>"^^rdf:HTML .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/1323>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“When the new government in Alberta speaks of an assertive, “war room” approach to communicating the province’s interests and countering biased criticisms, it’s fair to ask, who can blame them? Everything else has been tried. For the good of the environment and Canadian economic health, the task of standing strong cannot commence soon enough.";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/1323/source/24>;
        schema:author            <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/entity/stewart-muir/>;
        schema:claimInterpreter  <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:inLanguage        "English"^^schema:Text;
        schema:publisher         <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:url               "https://www.desmog.com/stewart-muir/" .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/1322/source/>
        rdf:type         schema:CreativeWork;
        schema:citation  ""^^rdf:HTML .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/1322>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“Launching lawsuits against oil and gas companies will do nothing to take on climate change. It is a feel-good PR exercise about winning points with voters that will stall climate-change action for years. It also ignores that they rely on oil and gas to operate their cities,” Muir added.";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/1322/source/>;
        schema:author            <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/entity/stewart-muir/>;
        schema:claimInterpreter  <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:inLanguage        "English"^^schema:Text;
        schema:publisher         <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:url               "https://www.desmog.com/stewart-muir/" .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/1321/source/20>
        rdf:type         schema:CreativeWork;
        schema:citation  "“<a href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20220902184909/https://macdonaldlaurier.ca/the-coming-energy-crisis-how-did-things-get-so-bad-so-fast-stewart-muir-and-margareta-dovgal-for-inside-policy/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=the-coming-energy-crisis-how-did-things-get-so-bad-so-fast-stewart-muir-and-margareta-dovgal-for-inside-policy\" data-wpel-link=\"external\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"external noopener noreferrer\">The coming energy crisis: How did things get so bad, so fast? Stewart Muir and Margareta Dovgal for Inside Policy</a>,” <em>Macdonald-Laurier Institute</em>, August 31, 2022. Archived November 30, 2022. Archive URL: <a href=\"https://archive.ph/REO1l\" data-wpel-link=\"external\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"external noopener noreferrer\">https://archive.ph/REO1l</a>"^^rdf:HTML .

