<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/1165>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“And it also had a impact on nuclear power as well. Lots of nuclear plants have closed as a result of so many renewables on the grid. Because you can’t slow down a nuclear power plant without de-stabilizing it. You can do that with coal or natural gas, so one of the main negative repercussions of these policies is that they are getting rid […] if they are supposed to be limiting CO2 emissions and they are taking nuclear power off the grid, its, eh, pretty questionable whether your goals are aligning or the results of your policies are aligning with your goals.”";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/1165/source/>;
