<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/1136>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“[I]t inaccurately, in my view, presents a view of climate change that is dominated by the emission of carbon dioxide and a few other greenhouse gases,” Pielke wrote. “Indeed, in my opinion, the committee, under the direction of Gerald North with the writing subgroup led by Susan Hassol, was clearly motivated to produce a statement of this one particular view. My viewpoint is that under this leadership, other views were never give an adequate opportunity to be discussed.”";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/1136/source/>;
        schema:author            <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/entity/roger-pielke-sr/>;
        schema:claimInterpreter  <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:inLanguage        "English"^^schema:Text;
        schema:publisher         <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:url               "https://www.desmog.com/roger-pielke-sr/" .

