<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/912>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "To avoid electricity brown-outs, then black-outs, fuel shortages and soaring costs, we must derail the climate change scaremongering that is driving these dangerous trends. If we don’t, unemployment will rise quickly as companies and governments face debilitating energy costs. Collateral economic damage will be most severe in rural areas that are already seriously challenged. Reduced funding for education, health care, defense, science and worthwhile environmental programs will follow, eventually threatening national security.";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/912/source/104>;
        schema:author            <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/entity/tom-harris/>;
        schema:claimInterpreter  <http://desmog.com/>;
