<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/865>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“Judith Curry said of Hurricane Irma last week: ‘The surprising thing about this development into a major hurricane was that it developed over relatively cool waters in the Atlantic, 26.5C, when the rule of thumb is 28.5C for a major hurricane’. So it was not exceptional warmth, but exceptionally low wind shear (high-altitude wind) that led to Irma’s birth.”";
