        rdf:type         schema:CreativeWork;
        schema:citation  "Matt Ridley. “<a href=\"http://www.thetimes.co.uk/edition/comment/weve-become-a-nation-paralysed-by-protest-8w7n3n2f5\" data-wpel-link=\"external\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"external noopener noreferrer\">We’ve become a nation paralysed by protest</a>,” <em>The Times</em>, Ocrober 17, 2016. Archived .pdf on file at&nbsp;Desmog."^^rdf:HTML .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/832>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“[Fracking] has been tested tens of thousands of times in America with very few environmental problems. In that decade, America has used this technique to smash the oil and gas price, transform its economy and cut its carbon emissions. We’ve spent the decade in a futile attempt to placate a handful of implacable green&nbsp;fanatics.”";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/832/source/42>;
        schema:author            <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/entity/matt-ridley/>;
        schema:claimInterpreter  <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:inLanguage        "English"^^schema:Text;
        schema:publisher         <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:url               "https://www.desmog.com/matt-ridley/" .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/831/source/41>
        rdf:type         schema:CreativeWork;
        schema:citation  "Matt Ridley. “<a href=\"http://www.spectator.co.uk/2016/10/the-world-is-getting-greener-why-does-no-one-want-to-know/\" data-wpel-link=\"external\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"external noopener noreferrer\">The world is getting greener. Why does no one want to know?</a>” <em>The Spectator</em>, October 22, 2016. Archive.is <span class=\"caps\">URL</span>: <a href=\"https://archive.is/b8B7c\" data-wpel-link=\"external\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"external noopener noreferrer\">https://archive.is/b8B7c</a>"^^rdf:HTML .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/831>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“So far, the benefits of global greening have been greater than expected, while the costs of global warming have been smaller than expected and the price of reducing carbon dioxide emissions has been higher than expected. That price is falling more heavily on poor than on rich people. The evidence suggests that this imbalance will persist for most of this century, perhaps longer. It is time for a rethink,” Ridley ";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/831/source/41>;
        schema:author            <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/entity/matt-ridley/>;
        schema:claimInterpreter  <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:inLanguage        "English"^^schema:Text;
        schema:publisher         <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:url               "https://www.desmog.com/matt-ridley/" .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/830/source/40>
        rdf:type         schema:CreativeWork;
        schema:citation  "“<a href=\"http://web.archive.org/web/20180225190757/http://www.rationaloptimist.com/blog/the-mis-selling-of-the-paris-climate-treaty/\" rel=\"nofollow external noopener noreferrer\" data-wpel-link=\"external\" target=\"_blank\"><span class=\"caps\">THE</span> <span class=\"caps\">PARIS</span> <span class=\"caps\">CLIMATE</span> <span class=\"caps\">TREATY</span> <span class=\"caps\">IS</span> <span class=\"caps\">WEAK</span>, <span class=\"caps\">SO</span> <span class=\"caps\">WHY</span> <span class=\"caps\">DO</span> <span class=\"caps\">CLIMATE</span> <span class=\"caps\">ACTIVISTS</span> <span class=\"caps\">DEFEND</span> <span class=\"caps\">IT</span>?</a>“&nbsp;<em>MattRidley</em>, May 9, 2017. Archived February 25, 2018. Archive.is <span class=\"caps\">URL</span>: <a href=\"https://archive.is/ysZuV\" data-wpel-link=\"external\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"external noopener noreferrer\">https://archive.is/ysZuV</a>"^^rdf:HTML .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/830>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“Thus Paris embodies precisely what the green movement worried about after Copenhagen: that a weak and non-binding agreement would be worse than futile. Yet the disastrous Kyoto story is repeating itself; adherence to Paris has become a totem of global determination to tackle climate change while the agreement seems purpose-built to prevent the very economic sophistication on which any low-carbon future depends.”";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/830/source/40>;
        schema:author            <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/entity/matt-ridley/>;
        schema:claimInterpreter  <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:inLanguage        "English"^^schema:Text;
        schema:publisher         <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:url               "https://www.desmog.com/matt-ridley/" .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/829/source/39>
        rdf:type         schema:CreativeWork;
        schema:citation  "Paul Karp. “<a href=\"http://web.archive.org/web/20180225191009/https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2017/may/21/experts-reject-bjorn-lomborg-centres-view-that-2c-warming-target-not-worth-it\" data-wpel-link=\"external\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"external noopener noreferrer\">Experts reject Bjørn Lomborg’s view on 2C warming target</a>,” <em>The Guardian</em>, May 20, 2017. Archived February 25, 2018. Archive.is <span class=\"caps\">URL</span>: <a href=\"https://archive.is/m5Ktx\" data-wpel-link=\"external\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"external noopener noreferrer\">https://archive.is/m5Ktx</a>"^^rdf:HTML .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/829>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“Who could disagree? Lomborg wants Trump to can the Paris agreement, which he rightly judges to be a feelgood gesture that distracts attention from aggressive research into low-emitting, cost-effective energy technologies, which is the only realistic way to reduce fossil fuel&nbsp;consumption.";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/829/source/39>;
        schema:author            <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/entity/matt-ridley/>;
        schema:claimInterpreter  <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:inLanguage        "English"^^schema:Text;
        schema:publisher         <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:url               "https://www.desmog.com/matt-ridley/" .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/828/source/38>
        rdf:type         schema:CreativeWork;
        schema:citation  "“<a href=\"http://web.archive.org/web/20180225190757/http://www.rationaloptimist.com/blog/the-mis-selling-of-the-paris-climate-treaty/\" data-wpel-link=\"external\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"external noopener noreferrer\">THE PARIS CLIMATE TREATY IS WEAK, SO WHY DO CLIMATE ACTIVISTS DEFEND IT?</a>“&nbsp;<em>MattRidley</em>, May 9, 2017. Archived February 25, 2018. Archive.is URL: <a href=\"https://archive.is/ysZuV\" data-wpel-link=\"external\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"external noopener noreferrer\">https://archive.is/ysZuV</a>"^^rdf:HTML .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/828>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“Who could disagree? Lomborg wants Trump to can the Paris agreement, which he rightly judges to be a feelgood gesture that distracts attention from aggressive research into low-emitting, cost-effective energy technologies, which is the only realistic way to reduce fossil fuel&nbsp;consumption.";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/828/source/38>;
