<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/810>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“[C]ap-and-trade is a bureaucrat’s dream. Carbon is among the most abundant natural elements, and carbon dioxide is central to all life. As MIT climate scientist Dr. Richard Lindzen wrote, ‘If you control carbon, you control life.’” So predictably, advocates of big central government not only want to regulate carbon and the ability to buy and sell it, they also want to tax that right,” Walcher wrote in a ";
