<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/759/source/19>
        rdf:type         schema:CreativeWork;
        schema:citation  "“<a href=\"https://archive.is/xUSZ1\" data-wpel-link=\"external\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"external noopener noreferrer\">Thank God for the Atom Bomb</a>,” <em>The Wall Street Journal</em>, August 3, 2015. Archived April 17,&nbsp;2017."^^rdf:HTML .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/759>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“The bomb turned the empire of the sun into a nation of peace activists,” Stephens wrote. “Modern Japan is a testament to the benefits of total defeat, to stripping a culture prone to violence of its martial pretenses. Modern Hiroshima is a testament to human resilience in the face of catastrophe. It is a testament, too, to an America that understood moral certainty and even a thirst for revenge were not obstacles to magnanimity. In some ways they are the precondition for it.”";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/759/source/19>;
        schema:author            <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/entity/bret-stephens/>;
        schema:claimInterpreter  <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:inLanguage        "English"^^schema:Text;
        schema:publisher         <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:url               "https://www.desmog.com/bret-stephens/" .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/758/source/16>
        rdf:type         schema:CreativeWork;
        schema:citation  "“Bret Stephens. “<a href=\"https://archive.is/rJRNi\" data-wpel-link=\"external\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"external noopener noreferrer\">What’s the Next ‘Global Warming’?</a>“&nbsp;<em>Wall Street Journal</em>, April 6, 2010. Archived April 17,&nbsp;2017."^^rdf:HTML .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/758>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "He concluded with a proposal for “a readers’ contest to invent the next panic. It must involve something ubiquitous, invisible to the naked eye, and preferably mass-produced. And the solution must require taxes, regulation, and other changes to civilization as we know it.”";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/758/source/16>;
        schema:author            <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/entity/bret-stephens/>;
        schema:claimInterpreter  <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:inLanguage        "English"^^schema:Text;
        schema:publisher         <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:url               "https://www.desmog.com/bret-stephens/" .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/757/source/15>
        rdf:type         schema:CreativeWork;
        schema:citation  "“Bret Stephens. “<a href=\"https://archive.is/rJRNi\" data-wpel-link=\"external\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"external noopener noreferrer\">What’s the Next ‘Global Warming’?</a>“&nbsp;<em>Wall Street Journal</em>, April 6, 2010. Archived April 17,&nbsp;2017."^^rdf:HTML .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/757>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“So global warming is dead, nailed into its coffin one devastating disclosure, defection and re-evaluation at a time. Which means that pretty soon we’re going to need another apocalyptic scare to take its place,” he&nbsp;wrote.";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/757/source/15>;
        schema:author            <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/entity/bret-stephens/>;
        schema:claimInterpreter  <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:inLanguage        "English"^^schema:Text;
        schema:publisher         <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:url               "https://www.desmog.com/bret-stephens/" .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/756/source/14>
        rdf:type         schema:CreativeWork;
        schema:citation  "Bret Stephens. “<a href=\"http://web.archive.org/web/20150215092846/https://www.wsj.com/articles/SB10001424052970203935604577066183761315576\" data-wpel-link=\"external\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"external noopener noreferrer\">The Great Global Warming Fizzle</a>,” <em>The Wall Street Journal, </em>November 29, 2011. Archived February 15, 2015. Archive.is <span class=\"caps\">URL</span>: <a href=\"http://archive.is/ZVHKv\" data-wpel-link=\"external\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"external noopener noreferrer\">http://archive.is/<span class=\"caps\">ZVHK</span>v</a>"^^rdf:HTML .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/756>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "As with religion, it is presided over by a caste of spectacularly unattractive people pretending to an obscure form of knowledge that promises to make the seas retreat and the winds abate. As with religion, it comes with an elaborate list of virtues, vices and indulgences. As with religion, its claims are often non-falsifiable, hence the convenience of the term “climate change” when thermometers don’t oblige the expected trend lines. As with religion, it is harsh toward skeptics, heretics and other “deniers.” And as with religion, it is susceptible to the earthly temptations of money, power, politics, arrogance and deceit.”&nbsp;";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/756/source/14>;
        schema:author            <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/entity/bret-stephens/>;
        schema:claimInterpreter  <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:inLanguage        "English"^^schema:Text;
        schema:publisher         <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:url               "https://www.desmog.com/bret-stephens/" .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/755/source/13>
        rdf:type         schema:CreativeWork;
        schema:citation  "Bret Stephens. “<a href=\"http://web.archive.org/web/20150215092846/https://www.wsj.com/articles/SB10001424052970203935604577066183761315576\" data-wpel-link=\"external\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"external noopener noreferrer\">The Great Global Warming Fizzle</a>,” <em>The Wall Street Journal, </em>November 29, 2011. Archived February 15, 2015. Archive.is <span class=\"caps\">URL</span>: <a href=\"http://archive.is/ZVHKv\" data-wpel-link=\"external\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"external noopener noreferrer\">http://archive.is/<span class=\"caps\">ZVHK</span>v</a>"^^rdf:HTML .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/755>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“Consider the case of global warming, another system of doomsaying prophecy and faith in things&nbsp;unseen.";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/755/source/13>;
