<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/672>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“The responsible, conservative answer is to review the controversy over the climate change scandals, the majority opinion – that the planet is warming some but we don’t know how much, that humans contribute to the warming, but we don’t know by how much, and that we don’t know if it will be harmful or if there’s anything we can do about it – and a cautious preference for reducing greenhouse gases but not via a carbon tax or a cap-and-trade system that cannot work even if it was necessary because the world’s biggest emitters aren’t buying it nor should they.”";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/672/source/10>;
        schema:author            <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/entity/hugh-hewitt/>;
