<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/656>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“If the case for emission cutbacks is weaker than the public has been led to believe, the claim of a double dividend is on even shakier ground. There really is a consensus in this literature, and it is that carbon taxes cause more economic damage than generic taxes do on labor or capital, so that in general even a revenue-neutral carbon tax swap would probably reduce economic&nbsp;growth.”";
