<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/628>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“What we really don’t want to do, I think, is impose policies that would deny [Catholics in parts of the world vulnerable to climate change] access to electricity or make their access to electricity more difficult. And that’s were I think that’s where the Pope needs to be very, very careful here because if he favors policies that will ultimately put some of the good things about modern life out of reach of the most vulnerable, he will ultimately wind up perpetuating poverty and putting himself behind policies that will lead to shorter life expectancies and that that’s something I don’t think any of us want.”";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/628/source/>;
        schema:author            <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/entity/bonner-cohen/>;
        schema:claimInterpreter  <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:inLanguage        "English"^^schema:Text;
