<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/493>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“Climate change is real, Reform UK believes we must adapt, rather than foolishly think you can stop it. We are proud to be the only party to understand that economic growth depends on cheap domestic energy and we are proud that we are the only party that are climate science realists, realising you can not stop the power of the sun, volcanoes or sea level oscillation. The deniers are those who continually gaslight the public into thinking you can stop these powerful natural forces. We must use the energy under our feet, rather than send our money and jobs abroad.”";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/493/source/>;
        schema:author            <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/entity/reform-uk/>;
