<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/238>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“Unoccupied habitat is habitat that is not currently occupied by a listed species. To deal with the anticipated effects from climate change, the Service and NOAA Fisheries are proposing changes to their regulations that would vastly expand their authority to designate unoccupied areas as critical habitat. By changing a few words in a regulation, the Services would fundamentally alter the role that the designation of unoccupied areas has historically played in the ESA regulatory scheme.";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/238/source/61>;
        schema:author            <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/entity/david-bernhardt/>;
        schema:claimInterpreter  <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:inLanguage        "English"^^schema:Text;
        schema:publisher         <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:url               "https://www.desmog.com/david-bernhardt/" .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/237/source/60>
        rdf:type         schema:CreativeWork;
        schema:citation  "<a id=\"s39\" name=\"s39\" href=\"http://web.archive.org/web/20181219021714/https://naturalresources.house.gov/uploadedfiles/disclosure_bernhardt.pdf\" data-wpel-link=\"external\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"external noopener noreferrer\">“COMMITTEE ON NATURAL RESOURCES 114 th Congress Disclosure Form” (PDF)</a>, <em>House Committee on Natural Resources, </em>April 19, 2016."^^rdf:HTML .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/237>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“David Bernhardt has worked on Endangered Species Act matters for over twenty years; including while serving as the Solicitor of the Department of the Interior, as an attorney in private practice, and as a congressional aide. David has counseled the Secretary of the Interior and other Interior policymakers to help make challenging ESA decisions. He was also tasked with implementing and defending those decisions. In private practice, David has litigated against the federal agencies when failing to administer the act to protect species, as well as when administering the law in an arbitrary and capricious way. He also has extensive experience working with the Services to develop conservation plans, habitat conservation plans, and multi- species conservation plans.”";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/237/source/60>;
        schema:author            <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/entity/david-bernhardt/>;
        schema:claimInterpreter  <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:inLanguage        "English"^^schema:Text;
        schema:publisher         <http://desmog.com/>;
        schema:url               "https://www.desmog.com/david-bernhardt/" .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/236/source/49>
        rdf:type         schema:CreativeWork;
        schema:citation  "Darryl Fears. “<a href=\"https://www.washingtonpost.com/climate-environment/2019/04/11/senate-confirms-former-oil-gas-lobbyist-david-bernhardt-secretary-interior/?noredirect=on&amp;utm_term=.73783864a1d7\" data-wpel-link=\"external\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"external noopener noreferrer\">Senate confirms former oil and gas lobbyist David Bernhardt as interior secretary</a>,” <em>The Washington Post</em>, April 11, 2019. <a href=\"http://web.archive.org/web/20190411200947/https://www.washingtonpost.com/climate-environment/2019/04/11/senate-confirms-former-oil-gas-lobbyist-david-bernhardt-secretary-interior/?noredirect=on&amp;utm_term=.73783864a1d7\" data-wpel-link=\"external\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"external noopener noreferrer\">Archived April 11, 2019</a>. Archive.fo URL: <a href=\"https://archive.fo/3OZDg\" data-wpel-link=\"external\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"external noopener noreferrer\">https://archive.fo/3OZDg</a>"^^rdf:HTML .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/236>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“We are deeply disappointed that the Senate decided to confirm the Secretary of Interior with a record full of ethical conflicts and unwavering allegiance to the oil and gas industry,” said Rappaport. Interior “badly needs leadership that restores the public’s trust in its mission to conserve our natural resources, not more of the same failed policies and ethical challenges that have plagued the department under this administration.”";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/236/source/49>;
        schema:author            <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/entity/david-bernhardt/>;
