<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/149>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“Bryce complained that the new rules would allow wind energy producers to kill or injure up to 4,200 eagles per year and hyped data showing that wind turbines were responsible for about 573,000 total bird deaths (not just eagles) in 2012. But as the Daily Kos piece explained, it is misleading to cite these figures without explaining that wind turbines are responsible for only ‘about 3 percent of human-caused eagle deaths’&nbsp;and that other factors – including the oil and gas industry and climate change – are a much greater threat to birds than wind&nbsp;energy.”";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/149/source/35>;
