<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/113/source/79>
        rdf:type         schema:CreativeWork;
        schema:citation  "Lisa Graves. “<a href=\"http://www.prwatch.org/news/2012/06/11590/trained-koch-daily-caller-claims-fake-rebuttal-cmd-alec-role-promoting-stand-your\" data-wpel-link=\"external\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"external noopener noreferrer\">Trained on Koch: Daily Caller Claims Fake Rebuttal of CMD on ALEC Role Promoting ‘Stand Your Ground’ Laws</a>,” <em>PR Watch</em>, June 18, 2012. <a href=\"http://web.archive.org/web/20170324173649/http://www.prwatch.org/news/2012/06/11590/trained-koch-daily-caller-claims-fake-rebuttal-cmd-alec-role-promoting-stand-your\" data-wpel-link=\"external\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"external noopener noreferrer\">Archived March 24, 2017</a>. Archive.is URL: <a href=\"https://archive.is/D7Sk8\" data-wpel-link=\"external\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"external noopener noreferrer\">https://archive.is/D7Sk8</a>"^^rdf:HTML .

<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/113>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“Had Bastasch done any original research about CMD’s actual original reporting on SYG, he would have seen that CMD is the research organization that documented how ALEC “ratified” the Florida SYG bill after it was signed into law […]” Lisa Graves wrote at CMD. “Bastasch’s piece raises a question about how Daily Caller fact-checks its stories. If undocumented assertions like those about CMD are passed off as news, the Daily Caller could be said to be acting with reckless disregard for the truth,” she adds.";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/113/source/79>;
        schema:author            <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/entity/michael-bastasch/>;
