<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/70>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“It’s perfectly reasonable that adding CO2 to the atmosphere could cause some warming, probably minor. This perfectly reasonably supposition was turned into unreasonable dogma by certain scientific disciplines that sensed an opportunity. They realized that if CO2 were inflated into the great Satan, it would be very beneficial for their careers,” Rogers ";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/70/source/12>;
