<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/48>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“The science of how the world’s climate works is very weak. The models used by the UN&nbsp;to predict changes have enormous gaps of knowledge. There is also very vigorous debate&nbsp;among scientists about whether or not levels of carbon dioxide cause global warming or&nbsp;are caused by it. In other words, we do not know if human generated carbon dioxide is significant or not. Many of us just want to think it is.”";
