<http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/10>
        rdf:type                 schema:Claim;
        schema:abstract          "“STATS began life in 1993 as an attempt to point out that statistical knowledge was essential to understanding the world; and as we relied on the news media for so much knowledge about the world, it was vital that journalists understood how to interpret statistics and report them accurately. Hence, the name of our newsletter: VitalStats.";
        schema:archivedAt        <http://data.open.ac.uk/climate-sense/claim/10/source/8>;
